ollowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/0d1b301347e706794b21537a24d3f78947ce5f55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T16:38:32Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T16:38:32Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"## Advanced Model Filtering — Complete ✅\n\nThe filter panel was hidden by default (`showFilters = signal(false)`). This has been fixed — changed to `signal(true)` in [`models-modal.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/models-modal/models-modal.component.ts:385) so the advanced filter panel is **visible by default** when you open the models modal.\n\n### How to Use\n1. Click the model selector button in the header to open the models modal\n2. The filter panel is now visible immediately below the search bar\n3. Available filters:\n   - **Provider chips** — click to filter by provider (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, etc.)\n   - **Capability pills** — 👁 Vision, 🔧 Tools, 📋 JSON, 🧠 Thinking, ⚡ Streaming, 🌐 Browser\n   - **Category chips** — 💻 Top Coding, 🧠 Top Reasoning, 💰 Budget\n   - **Context window presets** — 8K+, 32K+, 128K+, 200K+\n   - **Speed tier** — Any, ⚡ Fast, 🔄 Medium, 🐢 Slow\n   - **Max price input** — filter by max $/1M tokens\n   - **Sort dropdown** — Name, Price ↑↓, Context ↓, Speed ↓, Provider\n   - **Clear all filters** button resets everything\n4. You can collapse/expand the filter panel using the filter icon button next to the search bar\n\n### Files Delivered\n\n| File | Status | Purpose |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| [`docs/advanced-model-filtering-design.md`](docs/advanced-model-filtering-design.md) | New | Architecture design document |\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/lib/interfaces.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/interfaces.ts) | Modified | Extended `AIModel` + new `ModelFilter`, `ModelCapabilityFilter`, `ModelSortOption` types |\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-metadata.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-metadata.ts) | New | Curated model lookup tables (top-coding, reasoning, budget, fast, browser) |\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-mapper.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-mapper.ts) | New | API response → enriched `AIModel` mapper |\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-filter.utils.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-filter.utils.ts) | New | Pure filter/sort/count functions |\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/index.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/index.ts) | Modified | Updated barrel exports |\n| [`apps/shell/src/app/layout/models-modal/models-modal.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/models-modal/models-modal.component.ts) | Rewritten | Full filter panel UI with signal-based state, enriched model cards, 200ms search debounce, accessibility (aria-pressed), proper error handling |\n\nBuild verified: `nx build shell` passes cleanly.","tree":{"sha":"ef541fb8fdf8264f9f637aaad4bb0073f31bb612","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/ef541fb8fdf8264f9f637aaad4bb0073f31bb612"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/0d1b301347e706794b21537a24d3f78947ce5f55","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/0d1b301347e706794b21537a24d3f78947ce5f55","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKDBkMWIzMDEzNDdlNzA2Nzk0YjIxNTM3YTI0ZDNmNzg5NDdjZTVmNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/308b2f48ddd2cd3e9367da303e377d6a855e4cb0","sha":"308b2f48ddd2cd3e9367da303e377d6a855e4cb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/308b2f48ddd2cd3e9367da303e377d6a855e4cb0"}],"sha":"0d1b301347e706794b21537a24d3f78947ce5f55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/0d1b301347e706794b21537a24d3f78947ce5f55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/308b2f48ddd2cd3e9367da303e377d6a855e4cb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T16:29:54Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T16:29:54Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"## Advanced Model Filtering — Implementation Complete ✅\n\n### What Was Built\nA comprehensive 8-dimensional model filtering system for the Polyglot AI models modal, enabling users to filter 500+ AI models by price, context window, capabilities, speed, categories, and provider.\n\n### Files Created (4 new)\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| [`docs/advanced-model-filtering-design.md`](docs/advanced-model-filtering-design.md) | Architecture design document with ADRs, signal flow, and UI layout spec |\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-metadata.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-metadata.ts) | Curated lookup tables (`Set<string>`) for top-coding, top-reasoning, budget, fast, and browser-tool models + helper functions |\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-mapper.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-mapper.ts) | [`mapApiModelToAIModel()`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-mapper.ts:7) — converts raw OpenRouter API responses to enriched `AIModel` objects with pricing, capabilities, speed tier, and categories |\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-filter.utils.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-filter.utils.ts) | Pure functions: [`applyModelFilters()`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-filter.utils.ts:6), [`sortModels()`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-filter.utils.ts:62), [`countActiveFilters()`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/model-filter.utils.ts:86) |\n\n### Files Modified (3 updated)\n\n| File | Changes |\n|------|---------|\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/lib/interfaces.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/interfaces.ts) | Extended `AIModel` with `browserTools`, `maxCompletionTokens`, `modality`, `speedTier`, `categories`. Added `ModelFilter`, `ModelCapabilityFilter`, `ModelSortOption`, `DEFAULT_MODEL_FILTER` |\n| [`libs/shared/models/src/index.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/index.ts) | Updated barrel exports for all 4 library files |\n| [`apps/shell/src/app/layout/models-modal/models-modal.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/models-modal/models-modal.component.ts) | Complete rewrite with advanced filter panel, signal-based state, enriched model cards |\n\n### Filter Dimensions Implemented\n\n| Filter | UI Control | Signal Path |\n|--------|-----------|-------------|\n| 🔍 **Text search** | Debounced input (200ms) | `filterState().searchQuery` |\n| 🏢 **Provider** | Multi-select colored chips | `filterState().providers[]` |\n| 👁 **Vision** | Toggle pill | `filterState().capabilities.vision` |\n| 🔧 **Tools/Function Calling** | Toggle pill | `filterState().capabilities.functionCalling` |\n| 📋 **JSON Mode** | Toggle pill | `filterState().capabilities.jsonMode` |\n| 🧠 **Thinking/Reasoning** | Toggle pill | `filterState().capabilities.thinking` |\n| ⚡ **Streaming** | Toggle pill | `filterState().capabilities.streaming` |\n| 🌐 **Browser Tools** | Toggle pill | `filterState().capabilities.browserTools` |\n| 💻 **Top Coding** | Category chip | `filterState().categories[]` |\n| 🧠 **Top Reasoning** | Category chip | `filterState().categories[]` |\n| 💰 **Budget** | Category chip | `filterState().categories[]` |\n| 📏 **Context Window** | Preset buttons (8K+, 32K+, 128K+, 200K+) | `filterState().contextWindowMin` |\n| 🏎 **Speed Tier** | Radio buttons (Any/Fast/Medium/Slow) | `filterState().speedTier` |\n| 💲 **Max Price** | Number input ($/1M tokens) | `filterState().priceMax` |\n| 📊 **Sort** | Dropdown (Name, Price↑↓, Context↓, Speed↓, Provider) | `filterState().sortBy` |\n\n### Quality Gates Passed\n- ✅ **Build**: `nx build shell` passes cleanly\n- ✅ **Code Review**: 8 findings identified and all fixed (overlay click, duplicate escape handler, fetch error handling, search debounce, NaN pricing, aria-pressed accessibility, filter count accuracy, type-safe template refs)\n- ✅ **Angular Compliance**: Standalone component, OnPush, Signals only (no RxJS), `app` prefix, SCSS, Tailwind CSS v4\n- ✅ **Backward Compatible**: `selectModel()` output and `closeModal` emitter unchanged","tree":{"sha":"4e64cb8cb90e735d8faf7cd4fecaf1ee95ca6cb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/4e64cb8cb90e735d8faf7cd4fecaf1ee95ca6cb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/308b2f48ddd2cd3e9367da303e377d6a855e4cb0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/308b2f48ddd2cd3e9367da303e377d6a855e4cb0","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKDMwOGIyZjQ4ZGRkMmNkM2U5MzY3ZGEzMDNlMzc3ZDZhODU1ZTRjYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/dd1260c9f024660325d17d51cb26410ad679267a","sha":"dd1260c9f024660325d17d51cb26410ad679267a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/dd1260c9f024660325d17d51cb26410ad679267a"}],"sha":"308b2f48ddd2cd3e9367da303e377d6a855e4cb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/308b2f48ddd2cd3e9367da303e377d6a855e4cb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/dd1260c9f024660325d17d51cb26410ad679267a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T15:49:51Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T15:49:51Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"## 🏛️ Kilo Code AI Mode Ecosystem — Complete Overhaul & Expansion Done\n\n### 72 Modes Active in [`.kilocodemodes`](.kilocodemodes)\n\nAll 72 modes are now live in the project''s [`.kilocodemodes`](.kilocodemodes:1) file (3,071 lines, 72 unique slugs, zero duplicates). The original 12 modes were rewritten with dramatically enhanced prompts, and 60 entirely new specialist modes were created.\n\n### Files Created/Modified\n\n| Location | Files | Purpose |\n|----------|-------|---------|\n| [`.kilocodemodes`](.kilocodemodes) | 1 file, 3071 lines | **Active mode configuration** — all 72 modes registered and ready to use |\n| [`LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/) | 71 YAML files | Individual mode export files for reference and version control |\n| [`MANIFEST.md`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/MANIFEST.md) | 1 file | Master catalog with tier architecture, collaboration graphs, escalation paths |\n\n### Complete Mode Roster (72 modes across 8 tiers)\n\n**T0 Foundation (6):** `architect`, `code`, `ask`, `debug`, `orchestrator`, `review`\n\n**T1 Core Engineering (8):** `frontend-specialist`, `backend-specialist`, `fullstack-engineer`, `api-designer`, `code-reviewer`, `code-simplifier`, `code-skeptic`, `test-engineer`\n\n**T2 AI/ML & Research (9):** `ml-engineer`, `dl-researcher`, `nlp-llm-specialist`, `computer-vision`, `rl-engineer`, `ai-safety`, `prompt-engineer`, `rag-architect`, `agent-orchestrator`\n\n**T3 Data & Infrastructure (8):** `data-engineer`, `data-scientist`, `db-engineer`, `cloud-architect`, `devops-engineer`, `sre-engineer`, `observability-engineer`, `streaming-architect`\n\n**T4 Security & Compliance (5):** `security-engineer`, `pen-tester`, `threat-modeler`, `compliance-auditor`, `legal-reviewer`\n\n**T5 Specialized Engineering (10):** `compiler-engineer`, `embedded-iot`, `realtime-systems`, `edge-computing`, `blockchain-engineer`, `mobile-engineer`, `gaming-engineer`, `robotics-engineer`, `quantum-engineer`, `bioinformatics`\n\n**T6 Product & Design (9):** `product-manager`, `ux-designer`, `design-systems`, `accessibility-engineer`, `i18n-l10n`, `tech-writer`, `dx-engineer`, `docs-specialist`, `visual-interpreter`\n\n**T7 Leadership & Strategy (9):** `engineering-manager`, `open-source-strategist`, `competitive-intel`, `research-analyst`, `migration-strategist`, `performance-engineer`, `legacy-modernizer`, `finops-analyst`, `community-builder`\n\n**T-Meta Cross-Cutting (8):** `mode-architect`, `chaos-engineer`, `knowledge-graph`, `platform-engineer`, `api-gateway`, `monorepo-specialist`, `microservices-architect`, `angular-specialist`\n\n### Enhancement Highlights\n\n- Every mode has an authoritative `roleDefinition` (2-3 sentences, specific expertise, no hedging)\n- Every mode has numbered bold-header `customInstructions` with imperative directives\n- Every mode references project conventions from [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) where applicable\n- Every mode has structured output format specifications\n- Every mode has both positive (\"ALWAYS\") and negative (\"NEVER\") constraints\n- Every mode has a guiding principle motto\n- Tool groups follow principle of least privilege (review modes can''t edit code, planning modes write markdown only)\n- Escalation paths defined between modes for seamless collaboration","tree":{"sha":"27aa5cddf19112327ea40fe792ad706dc2487842","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/27aa5cddf19112327ea40fe792ad706dc2487842"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/dd1260c9f024660325d17d51cb26410ad679267a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/dd1260c9f024660325d17d51cb26410ad679267a","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKGRkMTI2MGM5ZjAyNDY2MDMyNWQxN2Q1MWNiMjY0MTBhZDY3OTI2N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/67c92baea00e99fc988921431e83cabd7497db75","sha":"67c92baea00e99fc988921431e83cabd7497db75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/67c92baea00e99fc988921431e83cabd7497db75"}],"sha":"dd1260c9f024660325d17d51cb26410ad679267a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/dd1260c9f024660325d17d51cb26410ad679267a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/67c92baea00e99fc988921431e83cabd7497db75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T15:46:17Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T15:46:17Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"## 🏛️ Kilo Code AI Mode Ecosystem — Complete Overhaul & Expansion\n\n### Mission Accomplished: 71 Mode Files + 1 Master Manifest\n\nI''ve conducted a comprehensive overhaul and strategic expansion of the entire Kilo Code AI mode ecosystem, transforming 12 basic modes into **71 world-class specialist modes** organized across 8 tiers, plus a master [`MANIFEST.md`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/MANIFEST.md) catalog.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Done\n\n**Phase 1 — Analysis**: Read and analyzed all 12 existing mode files, identifying weaknesses:\n- Vague `roleDefinition` fields lacking authority and specificity\n- Missing or minimal `customInstructions` (some had only 1-2 sentences)\n- Inconsistent tool group permissions (some modes had overly broad access)\n- No structured output formats defined\n- No escalation paths or collaboration protocols\n- Missing project-specific conventions from [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md)\n\n**Phase 2 — Enhancement of 12 Existing Modes**: Every original mode was rewritten with:\n- Authoritative, BLUF-style role definitions (2-3 sentences, specific expertise)\n- Numbered bold-header `customInstructions` sections with imperative directives\n- Structured output format specifications\n- Positive AND negative constraints (\"ALWAYS\" + \"NEVER\")\n- Project-specific rules from [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) (Angular Signals, Go conventions, Nx, Module Federation)\n- Escalation paths to other modes\n- Guiding principle mottos\n\n**Phase 3 — Creation of 59 New Specialist Modes** spanning every critical discipline:\n\n| Tier | Category | Count | Modes |\n|------|----------|-------|-------|\n| **T0** | Foundation | 6 | [`architect`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/architect-export.yaml), [`code`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/code-export.yaml), [`ask`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/ask-export.yaml), [`debug`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/debug-export.yaml), [`orchestrator`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/orchestrator-export.yaml), [`review`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/review-export.yaml) |\n| **T1** | Core Engineering | 8 | [`frontend-specialist`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/frontend-specialist-export.yaml), [`backend-specialist`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/backend-specialist-export.yaml), [`fullstack-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/fullstack-engineer-export.yaml), [`api-designer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/api-designer-export.yaml), [`code-reviewer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/code-reviewer-export.yaml), [`code-simplifier`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/code-simplifier-export.yaml), [`code-skeptic`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/code-skeptic-export.yaml), [`test-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/test-engineer-export.yaml) |\n| **T2** | AI/ML & Research | 9 | [`ml-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/ml-engineer-export.yaml), [`dl-researcher`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/dl-researcher-export.yaml), [`nlp-llm-specialist`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/nlp-llm-specialist-export.yaml), [`computer-vision`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/computer-vision-export.yaml), [`rl-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/rl-engineer-export.yaml), [`ai-safety`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/ai-safety-export.yaml), [`prompt-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/prompt-engineer-export.yaml), [`rag-architect`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/rag-architect-export.yaml), [`agent-orchestrator`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/agent-orchestrator-export.yaml) |\n| **T3** | Data & Infrastructure | 8 | [`data-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/data-engineer-export.yaml), [`data-scientist`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/data-scientist-export.yaml), [`db-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/db-engineer-export.yaml), [`cloud-architect`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/cloud-architect-export.yaml), [`devops-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/devops-engineer-export.yaml), [`sre-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/sre-engineer-export.yaml), [`observability-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/observability-engineer-export.yaml), [`streaming-architect`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/streaming-architect-export.yaml) |\n| **T4** | Security & Compliance | 5 | [`security-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/security-engineer-export.yaml), [`pen-tester`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/pen-tester-export.yaml), [`threat-modeler`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/threat-modeler-export.yaml), [`compliance-auditor`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/compliance-auditor-export.yaml), [`legal-reviewer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/legal-reviewer-export.yaml) |\n| **T5** | Specialized Engineering | 10 | [`compiler-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/compiler-engineer-export.yaml), [`embedded-iot`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/embedded-iot-export.yaml), [`realtime-systems`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/realtime-systems-export.yaml), [`edge-computing`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/edge-computing-export.yaml), [`blockchain-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/blockchain-engineer-export.yaml), [`mobile-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/mobile-engineer-export.yaml), [`gaming-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/gaming-engineer-export.yaml), [`robotics-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/robotics-engineer-export.yaml), [`quantum-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/quantum-engineer-export.yaml), [`bioinformatics`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/bioinformatics-export.yaml) |\n| **T6** | Product & Design | 9 | [`product-manager`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/product-manager-export.yaml), [`ux-designer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/ux-designer-export.yaml), [`design-systems`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/design-systems-export.yaml), [`accessibility-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/accessibility-engineer-export.yaml), [`i18n-l10n`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/i18n-l10n-export.yaml), [`tech-writer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/tech-writer-export.yaml), [`dx-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/dx-engineer-export.yaml), [`docs-specialist`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/docs-specialist-export.yaml), visual-interpreter (in .kilocodemodes) |\n| **T7** | Leadership & Strategy | 9 | [`engineering-manager`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/engineering-manager-export.yaml), [`open-source-strategist`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/open-source-strategist-export.yaml), [`competitive-intel`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/competitive-intel-export.yaml), [`research-analyst`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/research-analyst-export.yaml), [`migration-strategist`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/migration-strategist-export.yaml), [`performance-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/performance-engineer-export.yaml), [`legacy-modernizer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/legacy-modernizer-export.yaml), [`finops-analyst`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/finops-analyst-export.yaml), [`community-builder`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/community-builder-export.yaml) |\n| **T-Meta** | Cross-Cutting | 7 | [`chaos-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/chaos-engineer-export.yaml), [`knowledge-graph`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/knowledge-graph-export.yaml), [`platform-engineer`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/platform-engineer-export.yaml), [`api-gateway`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/api-gateway-export.yaml), [`monorepo-specialist`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/monorepo-specialist-export.yaml), [`microservices-architect`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/microservices-architect-export.yaml), [`angular-specialist`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/angular-specialist-export.yaml) |\n\n### Key Design Principles Applied\n\n1. **Project-Aware**: Every relevant mode references [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) conventions (Angular 21 Signals, Go chi router, Nx 22+, Module Federation, Supabase)\n2. **Principle of Least Privilege**: Tool groups are restricted per mode purpose — review modes can''t edit code, planning modes can only write markdown\n3. **Structured Output**: Every mode defines its output format (tables, reports, checklists)\n4. **Escalation Paths**: Every mode knows when to hand off to another specialist\n5. **Collaboration Protocol**: Inter-mode handoff document format defined in [`MANIFEST.md`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/MANIFEST.md)\n6. **Guiding Principles**: Every mode ends with a memorable motto that anchors its behavior\n\n### Files Created/Modified\n\n- **71 YAML mode files** in [`LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/)\n- **1 Master Manifest** at [`MANIFEST.md`](LLM-READY-AI_MODES-INSTRUCTIONS/kilo_modes/MANIFEST.md) with complete catalog, collaboration graphs, escalation paths, and quality standards\n\nTo activate any of these modes in the project, copy the desired mode entries from their YAML files into the root [`.kilocodemodes`](.kilocodemodes) file under the `customModes:` array.","tree":{"sha":"d580ab4d844b5bb660069aaf85be84479d970be7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/d580ab4d844b5bb660069aaf85be84479d970be7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/67c92baea00e99fc988921431e83cabd7497db75","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/67c92baea00e99fc988921431e83cabd7497db75","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKDY3YzkyYmFlYTAwZTk5ZmM5ODg5MjE0MzFlODNjYWJkNzQ5N2RiNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/0cb13c0f8a1e8072c1c59b3d525f5df4aef34e0d","sha":"0cb13c0f8a1e8072c1c59b3d525f5df4aef34e0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/0cb13c0f8a1e8072c1c59b3d525f5df4aef34e0d"}],"sha":"67c92baea00e99fc988921431e83cabd7497db75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/67c92baea00e99fc988921431e83cabd7497db75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/0cb13c0f8a1e8072c1c59b3d525f5df4aef34e0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T15:11:56Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T15:11:56Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"## Visual Interpreter Mode — Complete Configuration Delivered\n\n### Files Created/Modified\n\n1. **[`visual-interpreter.json`](visual-interpreter.json)** — Standalone JSON reference (11,268 chars of `customInstructions`)\n2. **[`.kilocodemodes`](.kilocodemodes)** — Updated YAML with `visual-interpreter` as the 3rd mode (alongside `code-skeptic` and `mode-architect`)\n\n### Mode Configuration Summary\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **`slug`** | `visual-interpreter` |\n| **`name`** | Visual Interpreter |\n| **`description`** | Analyze images and text into LLM-ready specs |\n| **`whenToUse`** | Use when the user provides screenshots, wireframes, mockups, diagrams, flowcharts, handwritten notes, architecture sketches, UI designs, or any visual reference that needs to be interpreted and converted into structured, actionable Markdown specifications. Also use when combining visual inputs with text descriptions to produce requirements documents, technical specs, or implementation briefs for downstream LLM consumption. |\n| **`source`** | `project` |\n\n### [`roleDefinition`](visual-interpreter.json:6) (2 sentences, 422 chars)\n\nEstablishes the AI as an expert visual analyst and requirements engineer who transforms images/screenshots/wireframes/mockups/diagrams/sketches into comprehensive, LLM-ready Markdown specifications. Combines pixel-level visual observation with deep technical inference.\n\n### [`customInstructions`](visual-interpreter.json:7) (11,268 chars, 9 sections)\n\n| Section | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| **1. Image Analysis Pipeline** | 4-layer systematic extraction: Structural Scan → Content Extraction → Relationship Mapping → Behavioral Inference |\n| **2. Text Description Integration** | Merging text + visual inputs, conflict detection with `⚠️ Discrepancy Detected` callouts, `[text-only]`/`[visual-only]` markers |\n| **3. User Needs Extraction** | WHY/WHAT/WHO/WHEN/HOW framework, functional/non-functional requirements, acceptance criteria, edge cases, when to ask vs. infer |\n| **4. Multi-Image Handling** | 5 relationship patterns: Sequential Steps, Alternative Views, System Components, Before/After, Mixed/Unclear |\n| **5. Output Format** | Complete LLM-ready Markdown template with 8 required sections (Title, Visual Analysis, Requirements, Intent, Tech Specs, Constraints, Open Questions, Action Items) |\n| **6. Confidence Indicators** | 5 mandatory markers: `[explicit]`, `[inferred]`, `[uncertain]`, `[text-only]`, `[visual-only]` |\n| **7. Quality Standards** | Self-contained, consistent terminology, no vague language, actionable, complete, priority-ordered |\n| **8. Special Input Types** | Handling for handwritten notes, architecture diagrams, flowcharts, ERDs, running application screenshots |\n| **9. Interaction Protocol** | When to produce output immediately vs. ask questions, file naming conventions |\n\n### [`groups`](visual-interpreter.json:7) (Principle of Least Privilege)\n\n| Group | Access | Justification |\n|-------|--------|---------------|\n| `read` | Unrestricted | Read existing files, project structure for context |\n| `edit` | Restricted: `\\.(md\\|mdc\\|mdx)$` | Write Markdown specification files only — no source code modification |\n| `browser` | Unrestricted | Image handling, visual reference access |\n| `mcp` | Unrestricted | Workspace exploration tools |\n| `command` | **Not granted** | No terminal commands needed for visual analysis |\n\n### Validation Checklist ✅\n\nAll 12 checks passed: slug format, uniqueness, roleDefinition quality, customInstructions structure, least privilege, fileRegex escaping, source field, JSON validity, YAML validity, string escaping, description present, whenToUse present.\n\n### Motto\n\n*\"If someone reads only my Markdown and never sees the original images, they should be able to build exactly what the user intended.\"*","tree":{"sha":"06ae470b0ee6054e88e362751265044119d2dd38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/06ae470b0ee6054e88e362751265044119d2dd38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/0cb13c0f8a1e8072c1c59b3d525f5df4aef34e0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/0cb13c0f8a1e8072c1c59b3d525f5df4aef34e0d","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKDBjYjEzYzBmOGExZTgwNzJjMWM1OWIzZDUyNWY1ZGY0YWVmMzRlMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/c6b895e0d1e94b8a18d2c15a532b72136f6e28f9","sha":"c6b895e0d1e94b8a18d2c15a532b72136f6e28f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/c6b895e0d1e94b8a18d2c15a532b72136f6e28f9"}],"sha":"0cb13c0f8a1e8072c1c59b3d525f5df4aef34e0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/0cb13c0f8a1e8072c1c59b3d525f5df4aef34e0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/c6b895e0d1e94b8a18d2c15a532b72136f6e28f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T15:01:56Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T15:01:56Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"## Mode Architect — Complete Custom Mode Delivered\n\n### What Was Created\n\nA production-ready **Mode Architect** custom mode for Kilo Code, purpose-built for creating, editing, refining, and managing other custom modes. The mode is deployed in two formats:\n\n### Files Produced\n\n1. **[`mode-architect.json`](mode-architect.json)** (16,465 chars) — Standalone JSON reference file with the complete mode configuration\n2. **[`.kilocodemodes`](.kilocodemodes)** (20,819 chars) — Updated project-level YAML config with `mode-architect` appended as the second mode (after `code-skeptic`), ready for Kilo Code to load immediately\n\n### Mode Specification Summary\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **`slug`** | `mode-architect` |\n| **`name`** | Mode Architect |\n| **`description`** | Design and manage Kilo Code custom modes |\n| **`whenToUse`** | Use when creating new custom modes, editing existing mode configurations, analyzing modes for improvements, designing tool group permissions, or producing `.kilocodemodes`/`.roomodes` files |\n| **`source`** | `project` |\n\n**`roleDefinition`** (3 sentences): Establishes the AI as Kilo Code''s definitive expert on custom mode design with encyclopedic knowledge of configuration anatomy, prompt engineering principles, tool group permissions, and file restriction patterns.\n\n**`customInstructions`** (14,600+ chars, 10 sections):\n1. **Complete Mode Anatomy** — All 8 fields (including `description` and `whenToUse`), 5 tool groups, `fileRegex` syntax, `.kilocodemodes`/`.roomodes` formats\n2. **Requirements Elicitation** — 4-phase systematic discovery process with specific questions\n3. **roleDefinition Writing Framework** — 3 templates, rules, anti-patterns\n4. **customInstructions Writing Framework** — Structure rules, section types, anti-patterns\n5. **Tool Group Selection Strategy** — Decision matrix, principle of least privilege, common patterns\n6. **Mode Analysis & Improvement** — Boundary violations, permission audit, instruction quality\n7. **Output Format** — Dual JSON + YAML output, validation checklist\n8. **Common Pitfalls & Edge Cases** — JSON escaping, YAML gotchas, slug conflicts (6 reserved: `code`, `architect`, `ask`, `debug`, `orchestrator`, `review`)\n9. **Mode Lifecycle Management** — Create, edit, version, share, split, merge, deprecate\n10. **Interaction Protocol** — When to elicit vs generate, analysis triggers\n\n**`groups`** (principle of least privilege):\n- `read` — unrestricted (read existing configs)\n- `edit` — restricted to `\\.(json|ya?ml|md|mdc|mdx)$` (mode config and documentation files only)\n- `command` — unrestricted (JSON validation, file checks)\n- `mcp` — unrestricted (workspace exploration)\n- No `browser` access (not needed)\n\n**Motto**: *\"A well-crafted mode is a force multiplier — vague modes produce vague results, precise modes produce precise results.\"*\n\n### Workflow Executed\n\n1. **Research** (Ask mode) — Read [`.kilocodemodes`](.kilocodemodes) and [`notes_for_prompt_builder.md`](services/prompt/internal/handlers/notes_for_prompt_builder.md) to understand the configuration format, existing patterns, and prompt construction principles (BLUF, token efficiency, imperative verbs, structured output)\n2. **Implementation** (Code mode) — Synthesized all research into the complete [`mode-architect.json`](mode-architect.json) with 10 comprehensive instruction sections\n3. **Critical Review** (Code Skeptic mode) — Identified 15 issues across 7 categories; 1 critical (deployment), 2 significant (missing schema fields), 4 minor, rest nitpicks\n4. **Fixes** (Code mode) — Addressed all significant+ issues: added `description`/`whenToUse` fields, updated mode anatomy to document 8 fields, added `review` to reserved slugs, integrated into [`.kilocodemodes`](.kilocodemodes) YAML\n5. **Validation** — Both JSON and YAML validated syntactically correct via Node.js and js-yaml","tree":{"sha":"52bb037a6693f541bef0fa8c95976ad05dad84ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/52bb037a6693f541bef0fa8c95976ad05dad84ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/c6b895e0d1e94b8a18d2c15a532b72136f6e28f9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/c6b895e0d1e94b8a18d2c15a532b72136f6e28f9","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKGM2Yjg5NWUwZDFlOTRiOGExOGQyYzE1YTUzMmI3MjEzNmY2ZTI4Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/51e1c436e1b459e64dc199a19e4c0dca20e11afa","sha":"51e1c436e1b459e64dc199a19e4c0dca20e11afa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/51e1c436e1b459e64dc199a19e4c0dca20e11afa"}],"sha":"c6b895e0d1e94b8a18d2c15a532b72136f6e28f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/c6b895e0d1e94b8a18d2c15a532b72136f6e28f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/51e1c436e1b459e64dc199a19e4c0dca20e11afa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T14:45:23Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T14:45:23Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"kilo code custum modes v1","tree":{"sha":"efc7d1f6885ba5ed46c0c625fdafd8180f1f6934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/efc7d1f6885ba5ed46c0c625fdafd8180f1f6934"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/51e1c436e1b459e64dc199a19e4c0dca20e11afa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/51e1c436e1b459e64dc199a19e4c0dca20e11afa","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKDUxZTFjNDM2ZTFiNDU5ZTY0ZGMxOTlhMTllNGMwZGNhMjBlMTFhZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/70a26c645df08385832aea67707af168f6f9ff93","sha":"70a26c645df08385832aea67707af168f6f9ff93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/70a26c645df08385832aea67707af168f6f9ff93"}],"sha":"51e1c436e1b459e64dc199a19e4c0dca20e11afa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/51e1c436e1b459e64dc199a19e4c0dca20e11afa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/70a26c645df08385832aea67707af168f6f9ff93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T14:11:00Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T14:11:00Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"All UI issues from the screenshots have been fixed across 7 files. All 3 projects (chat, models, shell) build successfully with zero errors.\n\n## Fix 1: \"AI is thinking...\" indicator during streaming\n\n**Problem:** The typing indicator remained visible while the AI was actively streaming its response.\n\n**Solution:** Introduced a new [`isThinking`](libs/shared/data-access/src/lib/chat-state.service.ts:10) signal in `ChatStateService` to differentiate between \"waiting for first response chunk\" and \"actively streaming content.\"\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| [`chat-state.service.ts`](libs/shared/data-access/src/lib/chat-state.service.ts) | Added `isThinking` signal |\n| [`chat.service.ts`](chat/src/app/services/chat.service.ts) | Sets `isThinking=true` on request start, `false` on first content delta |\n| [`chat-container.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-container/chat-container.component.ts) | Changed typing indicator condition from `isStreaming()` → `isThinking()` |\n\n## Fix 2: Model card description text cropping\n\n**Problem:** Description text was cut off mid-line without any visual indication.\n\n**Solution:** Added CSS `line-clamp` (4 lines max) with `-webkit-line-clamp`, `overflow: hidden`, and `text-overflow: ellipsis` in [`model-card.component.ts`](models/src/app/components/model-card/model-card.component.ts).\n\n## Fix 3: Low visibility / poor contrast text\n\n**Problem:** Text in the model browser had poor contrast against the dark background.\n\n**Solution:** Updated text colors across model browser components:\n- [`model-card.component.ts`](models/src/app/components/model-card/model-card.component.ts) — Description text → `#cbd5e1` (slate-300), model names → `text-slate-300`\n- [`provider-group.component.ts`](models/src/app/components/provider-group/provider-group.component.ts) — Provider names → `text-slate-300`, model counts → `text-slate-500`\n\n## Fix 4: Capability badges (Context, Streaming, Pricing)\n\n**Problem:** Model cards lacked capability badges showing context window, streaming support, and pricing category.\n\n**Solution:** Added pill-shaped badges in [`model-card.component.ts`](models/src/app/components/model-card/model-card.component.ts):\n- **Context** badge (cyan) — shows token count (e.g., \"1.0M tokens\")\n- **Streaming** badge (rose/pink) — shown when model supports streaming\n- **Pricing (per 1M tokens)** badge (yellow) — label above pricing grid\n- Added [`hasStreaming()`](models/src/app/components/model-card/model-card.component.ts) computed signal\n- [`model-registry.service.ts`](models/src/app/services/model-registry.service.ts) — Maps `capabilities` from API response\n\n## Fix 5: Pricing display with INPUT/OUTPUT labels\n\n**Problem:** Pricing showed two dollar amounts without labels, making it unclear which was input vs output.\n\n**Solution:** Redesigned pricing in [`model-card.component.ts`](models/src/app/components/model-card/model-card.component.ts) as a 2-column grid with clear **INPUT** and **OUTPUT** uppercase labels in slate-400, values in emerald-400 with subtle cell backgrounds.","tree":{"sha":"634594389c47e2a47466e211b39ec8f9ba9c5d5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/634594389c47e2a47466e211b39ec8f9ba9c5d5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/70a26c645df08385832aea67707af168f6f9ff93","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/70a26c645df08385832aea67707af168f6f9ff93","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKDcwYTI2YzY0NWRmMDgzODU4MzJhZWE2NzcwN2FmMTY4ZjZmOWZmOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/30f38b63ed0933925036caab3f1c31d47c6a2b08","sha":"30f38b63ed0933925036caab3f1c31d47c6a2b08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/30f38b63ed0933925036caab3f1c31d47c6a2b08"}],"sha":"70a26c645df08385832aea67707af168f6f9ff93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/70a26c645df08385832aea67707af168f6f9ff93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/30f38b63ed0933925036caab3f1c31d47c6a2b08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T13:11:32Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T13:11:32Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"All image suggestions have been implemented across 11 files. Build passes successfully (`npx nx build shell` — exit code 0).\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n### 1. Parameter Info Icons, Tooltips & Info Cards (Right Sidebar)\n\n**Files modified:**\n- [`param-slider.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/right-sidebar/basic-tab/param-slider.component.ts) — Added `emoji`, `description`, `example`, `synergy`, `minLabel`, `maxLabel` inputs. Each parameter now has an ℹ️ info button that toggles a collapsible info panel with \"What it does\", \"Example\", and \"⚡ Synergy\" sections (animated with max-height/opacity transitions). Emoji labels display before parameter names. Min/max labels show descriptive text (e.g., \"0 (Precise)\" / \"2 (Creative)\").\n- [`basic-tab.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/right-sidebar/basic-tab/basic-tab.component.ts) — All 5 sliders (🌡️ Temperature, 🎯 Top P, 📏 Max Tokens, 🔄 Frequency Penalty, 🆕 Presence Penalty) now pass rich metadata from the legacy app.\n- [`advanced-tab.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/right-sidebar/advanced-tab/advanced-tab.component.ts) — All 4 sliders (🔢 Top K, 📊 Min P, 🔁 Repeat Penalty, 🎲 Seed) pass metadata. Toggle descriptions updated to be more informative.\n\n### 2. Welcome Screen Redesign\n\n**File modified:**\n- [`chat-container.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-container/chat-container.component.ts) — Replaced the basic \"Ready to chat\" screen with a modern design featuring: animated gradient orb with pulsing glow and rotating ring, \"Polyglot AI\" gradient text heading, 3 glass-morphism feature cards (🧠 Multi-Model, ⚡ Real-time Streaming, 🎛️ Fine-tuned Control), gradient-bordered action buttons with hover glow, floating background orbs with CSS animations, and a subtle grid pattern.\n\n### 3. Double Toggle Fix\n\n**File modified:**\n- [`toggle-switch.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/right-sidebar/basic-tab/toggle-switch.component.ts) — Removed conflicting `class=\"toggle-switch\"` that was causing the CSS `::after` pseudo-element to create a second dot on top of the Tailwind-based span dot. Now uses only Tailwind classes (`bg-violet-500`/`bg-gray-600` + `translate-x-5`/`translate-x-1`). Also added `infoText` input and expandable info panel.\n\n### 4. Model Details Panel\n\n**Files modified:**\n- [`interfaces.ts`](libs/shared/models/src/lib/interfaces.ts) — Extended `AIModel` with `capabilities`, `contextWindow`, and richer `pricing` (cachedRead/cachedWrite).\n- [`model-registry.service.ts`](models/src/app/services/model-registry.service.ts) — Maps `pricing` and `contextWindow` from API. Added `expandedModelId` signal and `toggleModelDetails()` method.\n- [`model-card.component.ts`](models/src/app/components/model-card/model-card.component.ts) — Clicking a model expands a detail panel showing: description, context window (formatted as \"1.0M tokens\"), capability badges (⚡ Streaming, 👁️ Vision, 🧠 Thinking), and pricing table ($X.XX / 1M tokens).\n- [`provider-group.component.ts`](models/src/app/components/provider-group/provider-group.component.ts) — Passes `expandedModelId` and `expandToggle` through to model cards.\n- [`model-browser.component.ts`](models/src/app/components/model-browser/model-browser.component.ts) — Wires up expand toggle from registry service.\n\n### 5. Chat Input Textarea Fix\n\n**File modified:**\n- [`chat-input.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-input/chat-input.component.ts) — Changed max-height from 160px to 288px (~12 rows). Removed conflicting inline styles that caused visual glitch. Updated auto-resize to dynamically toggle `overflow-y` between hidden/auto. Textarea now properly resets height on send and auto-resizes after enhance.","tree":{"sha":"8489c265e27a1ef500d050426bdeab3f41dc8fc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/8489c265e27a1ef500d050426bdeab3f41dc8fc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/30f38b63ed0933925036caab3f1c31d47c6a2b08","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/30f38b63ed0933925036caab3f1c31d47c6a2b08","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKDMwZjM4YjYzZWQwOTMzOTI1MDM2Y2FhYjNmMWMzMWQ0N2M2YTJiMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/e7d649f380f63b87cd2dcda41451400d13fa2d15","sha":"e7d649f380f63b87cd2dcda41451400d13fa2d15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/e7d649f380f63b87cd2dcda41451400d13fa2d15"}],"sha":"30f38b63ed0933925036caab3f1c31d47c6a2b08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/30f38b63ed0933925036caab3f1c31d47c6a2b08"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/e7d649f380f63b87cd2dcda41451400d13fa2d15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T11:53:01Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T11:53:01Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"## All Issues Fixed — Summary\n\n### Phase 1: Chat Message Scroll (5 fixes)\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| [`main-layout.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/main-layout.component.ts:52) | Added `min-h-0` to `<main>` element |\n| [`entry.ts`](chat/src/app/remote-entry/entry.ts:8) | Added `host: { class: ''flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0'' }` |\n| [`chat-container.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-container/chat-container.component.ts:26) | Added host styling + changed root div `h-full` → `flex-1 min-h-0` + added `min-h-0` to message list wrapper |\n| [`message-list.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/message-list/message-list.component.ts:16) | Added `:host` styles + overflow-wrap rules for long text |\n\n### Phase 2: Right Sidebar Scroll Fix\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| [`right-sidebar.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/right-sidebar/right-sidebar.component.ts:45) | Added `min-h-0` to scrollable `div.flex-1.overflow-auto`, updated `:host` to `display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 0`, added `flex-1 min-h-0` to `<aside>` base classes |\n\n### Phase 3: Model Browser Scroll Fix\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| [`model-browser.component.ts`](models/src/app/components/model-browser/model-browser.component.ts) | Added `host: { class: ''flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0'' }`, changed root div `h-full` → `flex-1 min-h-0`, added `min-h-0` to scrollable container |\n| [`entry.ts`](models/src/app/remote-entry/entry.ts) | Added `host: { class: ''flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0'' }` for flex chain participation |\n\n### Phase 4: Enter/Shift+Enter Toggle\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| [`chat-input.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-input/chat-input.component.ts) | Added `enterToSend` signal, Tailwind-styled slide toggle with \"Swap\" label, dynamic `<kbd>` hints that reflect current mode, updated `onKeyDown()` to swap Enter/Shift+Enter behavior based on toggle state |\n\nTypeScript compilation passes cleanly for all three projects (shell, chat, models).","tree":{"sha":"dd33eb38a4bd341492622c97c27b9397ebc26e02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/dd33eb38a4bd341492622c97c27b9397ebc26e02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/e7d649f380f63b87cd2dcda41451400d13fa2d15","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/e7d649f380f63b87cd2dcda41451400d13fa2d15","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKGU3ZDY0OWYzODBmNjNiODdjZDJkY2RhNDE0NTE0MDBkMTNmYTJkMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/d6039dae83ad5354322ab7b3bea1cb346a22abac","sha":"d6039dae83ad5354322ab7b3bea1cb346a22abac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/d6039dae83ad5354322ab7b3bea1cb346a22abac"}],"sha":"e7d649f380f63b87cd2dcda41451400d13fa2d15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/e7d649f380f63b87cd2dcda41451400d13fa2d15"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/d6039dae83ad5354322ab7b3bea1cb346a22abac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T11:40:38Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T11:40:38Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"## Chat Scroll Fix — Complete\n\nFixed the chat message scrolling issue by repairing **5 breaks** in the flex height containment chain. The root cause was that flex children default to `min-height: auto`, preventing them from shrinking below content size, so `overflow-y: auto` on the scroll container never activated.\n\n### Files Modified\n\n| # | File | Change |\n|---|------|--------|\n| 1 | [`main-layout.component.ts`](apps/shell/src/app/layout/main-layout.component.ts:52) | Added `min-h-0` to `<main>` element |\n| 2 | [`entry.ts`](chat/src/app/remote-entry/entry.ts:8) | Added `host: { class: ''flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0'' }` |\n| 3a | [`chat-container.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-container/chat-container.component.ts:26) | Added `host: { class: ''flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0'' }` |\n| 3b | [`chat-container.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-container/chat-container.component.ts:43) | Changed root div from `h-full` → `flex-1 min-h-0` |\n| 3c | [`chat-container.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-container/chat-container.component.ts:134) | Added `min-h-0` to message list wrapper div |\n| 4 | [`message-list.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/message-list/message-list.component.ts:16) | Added `:host` styles (`display: block; height: 100%; min-height: 0`) + overflow-wrap rules for long text |\n\n### Fixed Flex Chain\n\n```\nbody (h-screen, overflow-hidden) ✅\n  └─ div.h-screen.flex-col ✅\n       └─ div.flex.flex-1.overflow-hidden ✅\n            └─ main.flex-1.flex-col.min-w-0.min-h-0 ✅ Fix 1\n                 └─ app-chat-entry (host: flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0) ✅ Fix 2\n                      └─ app-chat-container (host: flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0) ✅ Fix 3a\n                           └─ div.flex-col.flex-1.min-h-0 ✅ Fix 3b\n                                └─ div.flex-1.overflow-hidden.min-h-0 ✅ Fix 3c\n                                     └─ app-message-list (:host block h-full min-h-0) ✅ Fix 4\n                                          └─ div.h-full.overflow-auto ✅ NOW SCROLLS\n```\n\nTypeScript compilation verified clean for both `shell` and `chat` projects. No functionality was changed — only layout/styling fixes.","tree":{"sha":"5cfbd71f6e07bdfc299751805390fec41b2404d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/5cfbd71f6e07bdfc299751805390fec41b2404d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/d6039dae83ad5354322ab7b3bea1cb346a22abac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/d6039dae83ad5354322ab7b3bea1cb346a22abac","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKGQ2MDM5ZGFlODNhZDUzNTQzMjJhYjdiM2JlYTFjYjM0NmEyMmFiYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/91c9c604f88b760f0b4e4e94b052898c22185440","sha":"91c9c604f88b760f0b4e4e94b052898c22185440","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/91c9c604f88b760f0b4e4e94b052898c22185440"}],"sha":"d6039dae83ad5354322ab7b3bea1cb346a22abac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/d6039dae83ad5354322ab7b3bea1cb346a22abac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/91c9c604f88b760f0b4e4e94b052898c22185440/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T10:56:20Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T10:56:20Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"## Enhance Logic Updated — 4 Files Modified, Build Verified ✅\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n#### 1. [`chat.service.ts`](chat/src/app/services/chat.service.ts) — Core Enhance Logic\n- **Replaced system prompt** — The weak 5-rule prompt (~280 chars) was replaced with a comprehensive **Prompt Architect** system prompt (~2,500 chars) featuring:\n  - XML-structured output format (`<role>`, `<context>`, `<task>`, `<requirements>`, `<output_format>`, `<examples>`, `<variables>`)\n  - BLUF (Bottom Line Up Front) principle enforcement\n  - **Downstream thinking elimination** — explicit rules forcing the enhanced prompt to be so directive that the receiving AI executes immediately with zero internal deliberation\n  - \"No preamble, no reasoning, respond directly\" constraint auto-injected into requirements\n  - Ruthless optimization rules for code/writing tasks\n- **Removed user message prefix** — No longer sends `\"Enhance this prompt:\\n\\n\"` (redundant with system prompt)\n- **Increased `max_tokens`** from `2048` → `4096` (prevents truncation of XML-structured output)\n- **Fixed error handling** — Now throws on failure instead of silently returning original prompt\n\n#### 2. [`chat-input.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-input/chat-input.component.ts) — UI Component\n- **Added [`enhanceError`](chat/src/app/components/chat-input/chat-input.component.ts:159) input signal** — Receives error state from parent\n- **Added error `effect()`** — Resets `isEnhancing` to `false` when error occurs (fixes **spinner stuck bug** where the button stayed in \"Enhancing…\" state forever on failure)\n- **Added Mac keyboard shortcut** — `Cmd+Shift+E` now works alongside `Ctrl+Shift+E`\n\n#### 3. [`chat-container.component.ts`](chat/src/app/components/chat-container/chat-container.component.ts) — Parent Orchestrator\n- **Added [`enhanceError`](chat/src/app/components/chat-container/chat-container.component.ts:197) signal** with template binding `[enhanceError]=\"enhanceError()\"`\n- **Updated [`onEnhancePrompt()`](chat/src/app/components/chat-container/chat-container.component.ts:219)** — Sets `enhanceError(true)` on catch, shows error toast, auto-resets after 100ms\n\n#### 4. [`enhance.go`](services/prompt/internal/handlers/enhance.go) — Go Backend\n- **Replaced `promptArchitectSystem`** constant with the improved XML-structured prompt matching the frontend\n- **Changed temperature** from `0.7` → `0.3` (aligned with frontend for consistent behavior)\n- **Removed user message prefix** — Sends raw prompt directly\n\n### Key Improvements Over Previous Implementation\n| Aspect | Before | After |\n|--------|--------|-------|\n| System prompt quality | 5 generic rules (~280 chars) | XML-structured protocol with BLUF, thinking elimination (~2,500 chars) |\n| Downstream AI thinking | No guidance → AI wastes tokens reasoning | Explicit \"no preamble, respond directly\" constraints → immediate execution |\n| Error recovery | Spinner stuck forever on failure | Error signal resets UI, toast notification shown |\n| Max tokens | 2048 (truncation risk) | 4096 |\n| User message | Redundant prefix added | Raw text only |\n| Mac support | Ctrl+Shift+E only | Ctrl+Shift+E + Cmd+Shift+E |\n| Go backend alignment | Different prompt, temp 0.7 | Same prompt, temp 0.3 |","tree":{"sha":"a81058fe06044a64434cb291911333a91cdda348","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/a81058fe06044a64434cb291911333a91cdda348"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/commits/91c9c604f88b760f0b4e4e94b052898c22185440","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/91c9c604f88b760f0b4e4e94b052898c22185440","node_id":"C_kwDOR_lC99oAKDkxYzljNjA0Zjg4Yjc2MGYwYjRlNGU5NGIwNTI4OThjMjIxODU0NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commit/367e57e3a06db47efa110ff29302339a57c26de3","sha":"367e57e3a06db47efa110ff29302339a57c26de3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/367e57e3a06db47efa110ff29302339a57c26de3"}],"sha":"91c9c604f88b760f0b4e4e94b052898c22185440","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/91c9c604f88b760f0b4e4e94b052898c22185440"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5520338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ZeroStack","id":5520338,"login":"ZeroStack","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjAzMzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZeroStack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/commits/367e57e3a06db47efa110ff29302339a57c26de3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T10:23:16Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T10:23:16Z","email":"zerostack@users.noreply.github.com","name":"zerostack"},"message":"refactor(ui): redesign shell layout components and add right sidebar parameter tabs\n\n- Replace dynamic MFE loading in right sidebar with built-in tabbed\n  parameter dashboard (presets, basic, advanced, tokens tabs)\n- Rebrand API key modal from OpenRouter to Kilo with updated placeholder\n  and copy\n- Add proper label-for associations on login and register form inputs\n  for accessibility\n- Refactor models modal with inline search in header and checkmark for\n  selected model\n- Introduce Tailwind v4 @theme configuration and CSS custom properties\n  for consistent design tokens across shell styles\n- Add comprehensive global styles for chat MFE including markdown,\n  code blocks, glassmorphism, and responsive utilities\n- Enhance markdown pipe with link parsing and table rendering support\n- Update code-block component with improved copy feedback and styling\n- Add \"AI is thinking...\" label to typing indicator\n- Simplify app.spec.ts by removing NxWelcome references and using\n  provideRouter\n- Clean up header, left sidebar, and chat container styling for\n  consistency","tree":{"sha":"081a0182ad4343a229c76dd60d8f3b5cd4e09f00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aiEmployee-eu/polyglot-ai/git/trees/081a0182ad4343a229c76dd60d8f3b5cd4e09f00"},"url":"https://api.git