},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T10:25:19Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"ci: scope pipeline to changed project via DRY rules anchors\n\nRefactors .gitlab-ci.yml to extract path lists and rule blocks into\nreusable YAML anchors. Each of the 18 jobs now references its anchor\ninstead of repeating the same changes: pattern, which keeps the four\nstages (build/test/docker/deploy) in sync.\n\nBehaviour:\n- shared-ui/** or shell/** -> full pipeline runs (regression safety net)\n- mfe-payments/**, mfe-transactions/**, mfe-analytics-react/** -> only\n  the affected MFE pipeline runs, so each product team can ship without\n  blocking the other seven\n- .gitlab-ci.yml itself -> full pipeline (validates CI changes)\n\nAdds a workflow: block that enables merge_request_event pipelines and\nsuppresses the duplicate branch pipeline when a MR is open for that\nbranch.","tree":{"sha":"77aae7eb4d6f27b8c8a7ba9ad752c689b1851969","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/77aae7eb4d6f27b8c8a7ba9ad752c689b1851969"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/0fda0aea0dd71aba5aff91a7c537dd9d8f920bc4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/0fda0aea0dd71aba5aff91a7c537dd9d8f920bc4","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDBmZGEwYWVhMGRkNzFhYmE1YWZmOTFhN2M1MzdkZDlkOGY5MjBiYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/b9cac773b8582c890cdb49dd3e61be486b39cf66","sha":"b9cac773b8582c890cdb49dd3e61be486b39cf66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/b9cac773b8582c890cdb49dd3e61be486b39cf66"}],"sha":"0fda0aea0dd71aba5aff91a7c537dd9d8f920bc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/0fda0aea0dd71aba5aff91a7c537dd9d8f920bc4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/b9cac773b8582c890cdb49dd3e61be486b39cf66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T08:11:13Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T08:11:13Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"style(mfes): drop inline comments above CSP header","tree":{"sha":"45696ed64ba488279b3acf78ffc9a76c474e1225","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/45696ed64ba488279b3acf78ffc9a76c474e1225"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/b9cac773b8582c890cdb49dd3e61be486b39cf66","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/b9cac773b8582c890cdb49dd3e61be486b39cf66","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKGI5Y2FjNzczYjg1ODJjODkwY2RiNDlkZDNlNjFiZTQ4NmIzOWNmNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782","sha":"6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782"}],"sha":"b9cac773b8582c890cdb49dd3e61be486b39cf66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/b9cac773b8582c890cdb49dd3e61be486b39cf66"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/2c2e843424f9d02042ba06b69334418b9dc66819/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T08:09:59Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T08:09:59Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"test(e2e): add functional specs for filter, export and language toggle\n\nThree Playwright specs exercising real flows on the live stack, taking\nthe suite from smoke-only to functional:\n\n- transactions-filter: typing in the search input must shrink the\n  \"Filas filtradas\" stat card and clearing the form must restore it.\n- transactions-export: clicking \"Exportar Excel\" must fire a real\n  download event and surface the success alert; the worker keeps the\n  main thread responsive.\n- language-toggle: the header language button must swap the navigation\n  labels between English (default) and Spanish in both directions.\n\nAlso tightens the existing transactions smoke spec: getByText\n(''Transacciones'') was matching both the heading and the spinner label\n\"Cargando transacciones...\" in strict mode, so it now targets the\nheading role.\n\nIgnores test-results/ and playwright-report/ so future failures do not\nleak artifacts into commits.","tree":{"sha":"6ef7de971338206f83e55f959b2b07df3f084107","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/6ef7de971338206f83e55f959b2b07df3f084107"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/2c2e843424f9d02042ba06b69334418b9dc66819","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/2c2e843424f9d02042ba06b69334418b9dc66819","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDJjMmU4NDM0MjRmOWQwMjA0MmJhMDZiNjkzMzQ0MThiOWRjNjY4MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782","sha":"6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782"}],"sha":"2c2e843424f9d02042ba06b69334418b9dc66819","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/2c2e843424f9d02042ba06b69334418b9dc66819"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T07:52:38Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T07:52:38Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"Merge: 6 audit fixes pre-defense hardening","tree":{"sha":"a50fdaf37cdf6ff0a00e571538d7f839a0a5698a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/a50fdaf37cdf6ff0a00e571538d7f839a0a5698a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDZkYTBjMTMxODJiMTg3ZDMyYWM1YWY0OGM2MjFiZWEzNmZhYTc3ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055","sha":"29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/ec5e35fc220fbb4d31379d7130f4db7abecceb5e","sha":"ec5e35fc220fbb4d31379d7130f4db7abecceb5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/ec5e35fc220fbb4d31379d7130f4db7abecceb5e"}],"sha":"6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/6da0c13182b187d32ac5af48c621bea36faa7782"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/ec5e35fc220fbb4d31379d7130f4db7abecceb5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T07:34:28Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T07:43:24Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"fix(docker): build shared-ui dist before each Angular MFE build\n\nWhen mfe-payments, mfe-transactions and shell were refactored to consume\nshared-ui as a dist artifact (commit 46d814b), the CI was updated to\nbuild shared-ui first and pass its dist as an artifact between jobs, but\nthe Dockerfiles never got the equivalent step. With **/dist excluded by\n.dockerignore, the source-only COPY left ../shared-ui/dist empty inside\nthe build stage and npm run build failed resolving @capitalflow/shared-ui.\n\nThe four MFE/host stacks were green in CI because docker:* and deploy:*\njobs are explicit mocks (allow_failure: true with echo \"skipped\"), so\nthe broken Docker flow never surfaced. Now docker compose build works\nend-to-end for all five images (shell, mfe-analytics, mfe-payments,\nmfe-transactions, storybook).\n\nmfe-analytics-react already worked: it imports shared-ui SCSS from source\n(no Angular dependency on the dist), so its Dockerfile is unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"a50fdaf37cdf6ff0a00e571538d7f839a0a5698a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/a50fdaf37cdf6ff0a00e571538d7f839a0a5698a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/ec5e35fc220fbb4d31379d7130f4db7abecceb5e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/ec5e35fc220fbb4d31379d7130f4db7abecceb5e","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKGVjNWUzNWZjMjIwZmJiNGQzMTM3OWQ3MTMwZjRkYjdhYmVjY2ViNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/8a55f3591fde01664e793cce7147da018c1adbad","sha":"8a55f3591fde01664e793cce7147da018c1adbad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/8a55f3591fde01664e793cce7147da018c1adbad"}],"sha":"ec5e35fc220fbb4d31379d7130f4db7abecceb5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/ec5e35fc220fbb4d31379d7130f4db7abecceb5e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/8a55f3591fde01664e793cce7147da018c1adbad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T06:49:48Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T07:43:23Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"fix(mfes): add Content-Security-Policy header to each MFE nginx config\n\nThe shell nginx already shipped a strict CSP; the MFE nginx files were\nmissing the directive. Anyone hitting an MFE directly on its port\n(localhost:8082-8084 in docker-compose) had no CSP applied, which left\na gap in the vuln #6 mitigation claimed in the proposal.\n\nEach MFE now declares the same base CSP as the shell. frame-ancestors\nkeeps ''self'' and the local shell host so the MFE can still be loaded\nvia the reverse proxy; the host list is meant to be tightened per\nenvironment.","tree":{"sha":"4558db7ac8ee6cbb3157dfe95ea3801c115d5f07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/4558db7ac8ee6cbb3157dfe95ea3801c115d5f07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/8a55f3591fde01664e793cce7147da018c1adbad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/8a55f3591fde01664e793cce7147da018c1adbad","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDhhNTVmMzU5MWZkZTAxNjY0ZTc5M2NjZTcxNDdkYTAxOGMxYWRiYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/810b468cc8ff378fdebc36f37e5656b7f4b90573","sha":"810b468cc8ff378fdebc36f37e5656b7f4b90573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/810b468cc8ff378fdebc36f37e5656b7f4b90573"}],"sha":"8a55f3591fde01664e793cce7147da018c1adbad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/8a55f3591fde01664e793cce7147da018c1adbad"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/810b468cc8ff378fdebc36f37e5656b7f4b90573/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T06:49:30Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T07:43:23Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"test(e2e): make wysiwyg xss assertion explicit instead of tautological\n\nThe previous test relied on a side-effect: the dialog handler threw on\nalert and the body ended with expect(true).toBe(true). That reads as a\ntautology to anyone scanning the spec, and the test would silently pass\nif the handler ever failed to attach.\n\nThe handler now flips an alertFired flag and records the messages for\ndebugging; the test asserts explicitly that no dialog was triggered.\nSame coverage, clearer intent.","tree":{"sha":"3a62f8629ef5a68708337b8ad4ac257d3cc63e79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/3a62f8629ef5a68708337b8ad4ac257d3cc63e79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/810b468cc8ff378fdebc36f37e5656b7f4b90573","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/810b468cc8ff378fdebc36f37e5656b7f4b90573","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDgxMGI0NjhjYzhmZjM3OGZkZWJjMzZmMzdlNTY1NmI3ZjRiOTA1NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/88136435e22dbc81af108543394a911e71a67be0","sha":"88136435e22dbc81af108543394a911e71a67be0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/88136435e22dbc81af108543394a911e71a67be0"}],"sha":"810b468cc8ff378fdebc36f37e5656b7f4b90573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/810b468cc8ff378fdebc36f37e5656b7f4b90573"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/88136435e22dbc81af108543394a911e71a67be0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T06:49:20Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T07:43:23Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"chore(mfes): drop unused dompurify dependency from payments and transactions\n\ndompurify was declared in mfe-payments and mfe-transactions but never\nimported anywhere in their source. The shell and shared-ui''s\nSafeHtmlPipe are the only real consumers in the project.\n\nRemoved from both package.json and package-lock.json, along with the\norphaned @types/trusted-types optional dependency that came along with\nit. Bundle hygiene only; no behavioural change.","tree":{"sha":"e3ebe0a527d3f83983cff9daffcf79b9c6517734","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/e3ebe0a527d3f83983cff9daffcf79b9c6517734"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/88136435e22dbc81af108543394a911e71a67be0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/88136435e22dbc81af108543394a911e71a67be0","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDg4MTM2NDM1ZTIyZGJjODFhZjEwODU0MzM5NGE5MTFlNzFhNjdiZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/688de94216c2d1988783d6afa7fb56a5b930bf3d","sha":"688de94216c2d1988783d6afa7fb56a5b930bf3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/688de94216c2d1988783d6afa7fb56a5b930bf3d"}],"sha":"88136435e22dbc81af108543394a911e71a67be0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/88136435e22dbc81af108543394a911e71a67be0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/688de94216c2d1988783d6afa7fb56a5b930bf3d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T06:49:01Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T07:43:23Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): react cap-modal to signal changes via effect() + modal stack\n\nngOnChanges does not fire when a signal (model<boolean>) changes, so\nsetTimeModalOpen() and the body scroll lock only ran on the first\nrender. Replaced with an effect() that tracks showModal() and reacts on\nevery open/close transition.\n\nConcurrent modals also left document.body.style.overflow inconsistent:\nopen A, open B, close B unlocked the body while A was still open. A\nstatic openModalCount now releases the scroll lock only when the count\nreturns to zero, and DestroyRef.onDestroy decrements it if a component\nis torn down while still open.","tree":{"sha":"3ae7cb6b7be42f46ef90960483dfca7c8b9e85f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/3ae7cb6b7be42f46ef90960483dfca7c8b9e85f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/688de94216c2d1988783d6afa7fb56a5b930bf3d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/688de94216c2d1988783d6afa7fb56a5b930bf3d","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDY4OGRlOTQyMTZjMmQxOTg4NzgzZDZhZmE3ZmI1NmE1YjkzMGJmM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/5b5da4d63558324e517b563c0f7c713e4a19f650","sha":"5b5da4d63558324e517b563c0f7c713e4a19f650","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/5b5da4d63558324e517b563c0f7c713e4a19f650"}],"sha":"688de94216c2d1988783d6afa7fb56a5b930bf3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/688de94216c2d1988783d6afa7fb56a5b930bf3d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/5b5da4d63558324e517b563c0f7c713e4a19f650/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T06:48:46Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T07:43:23Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"fix(shared-ui): sanitize cap-tooltip innerHTML with safeHtml pipe\n\nThe four [innerHTML] bindings on titleTooltip and textTooltip now run\nthrough the SafeHtmlPipe (DOMPurify + DomSanitizer), in line with the\nlibrary policy of never binding raw HTML directly. Today the only\nconsumer is cap-input, which feeds tooltip text from trusted i18n\nstrings, so the change is defence-in-depth rather than a behaviour fix.","tree":{"sha":"9e6a6d2af1c94d16a7d76cddf26e7916ef4fe75e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/9e6a6d2af1c94d16a7d76cddf26e7916ef4fe75e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/5b5da4d63558324e517b563c0f7c713e4a19f650","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/5b5da4d63558324e517b563c0f7c713e4a19f650","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDViNWRhNGQ2MzU1ODMyNGU1MTdiNTYzYzBmN2M3MTNlNGExOWY2NTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055","sha":"29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055"}],"sha":"5b5da4d63558324e517b563c0f7c713e4a19f650","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/5b5da4d63558324e517b563c0f7c713e4a19f650"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T22:03:11Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T22:03:11Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"chore(shell): tighten initial bundle budgets to 550kB/700kB\n\nProduction build currently sits at 546.61 kB initial total, so the\nprevious 600 kB warning / 2 MB error window was too loose to act as\na regression guard. New values: 550 kB warning (close enough to fail\nfast on any non-trivial regression) and 700 kB error (keeps a sensible\nceiling well below the 800 kB target documented in the proposal for\nthe due-diligence milestone).","tree":{"sha":"d861c240462fa74133cd9d6ad1c71945196d7227","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/d861c240462fa74133cd9d6ad1c71945196d7227"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDI5ZmMzNTE1YzAxNDM0ZTUzYmUzMzY5NTk1NTdjMGVlN2QwZTcwNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/5bc9d9cdc6536b91ba0a243fd535b3070d0412de","sha":"5bc9d9cdc6536b91ba0a243fd535b3070d0412de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/5bc9d9cdc6536b91ba0a243fd535b3070d0412de"}],"sha":"29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/29fc3515c01434e53be336959557c0ee7d0e7055"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/5bc9d9cdc6536b91ba0a243fd535b3070d0412de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T22:03:02Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T22:03:02Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"feat(shell): add stored-XSS comments demo for briefing vuln #1\n\nAdds the fifth interactive security demo at /admin/comments mapping to\nvulnerability #1 of the external audit report (\"XSS in transaction\ncomments rendered directly to the DOM\"). Pattern mirrors the existing\ndocument-uploads and search-demo screens.\n\nThe demo seeds four transaction comments (the fourth one hostile, with\n<script>alert(\"XSS\")</script>) and exposes an input + \"Inject test\npayload\" button so the evaluator can confirm that user-typed payloads\nrender as literal text. Rendering is plain Angular interpolation; the\ncomponent uses OnPush, signal()/computed() and toSignal(valueChanges)\nto keep the \"Add\" button reactive against the FormControl.\n\nThe admin-landing matrix row briefing-01 moves from\nstatus=partial/demoRoute=null to status=mitigated/demoRoute=/admin/comments\nso the table now exposes 5 live demos for 5 of the 7 briefing\nvulnerabilities, with the remaining 2 (HttpOnly cookies, external SAST)\ndocumented as platform/Sprint controls.\n\nShell tests grow from 94 to 99 (5 new spec cases covering: component\ncreation, hostile seeded comment rendered as text, runtime-injected\npayload rendered as text, empty input guard, back navigation).","tree":{"sha":"2cb5f4fcf72a86f2b77c7240ba36039a8b8272c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/2cb5f4fcf72a86f2b77c7240ba36039a8b8272c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/5bc9d9cdc6536b91ba0a243fd535b3070d0412de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/5bc9d9cdc6536b91ba0a243fd535b3070d0412de","node_id":"C_kwDOR_2t3NoAKDViYzlkOWNkYzY1MzZiOTFiYTBhMjQzZmQ1MzViMzA3MGQwNDEyZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/5a6b094b349172407e8a40c0fc59d6c789119e7d","sha":"5a6b094b349172407e8a40c0fc59d6c789119e7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/5a6b094b349172407e8a40c0fc59d6c789119e7d"}],"sha":"5bc9d9cdc6536b91ba0a243fd535b3070d0412de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/5bc9d9cdc6536b91ba0a243fd535b3070d0412de"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commits/5a6b094b349172407e8a40c0fc59d6c789119e7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T17:43:03Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T17:43:03Z","email":"francisco.liebanas@nter.es","name":"FranciscoLiebanas"},"message":"fix: declare test type globals and fix directive null target","tree":{"sha":"0064d1832a0624ef16af9f20005baaf53644d318","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/trees/0064d1832a0624ef16af9f20005baaf53644d318"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/git/commits/5a6b094b349172407e8a40c0fc59d6c789119e7d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/franciscoliebanastalavera/expert/commit/5a6b094b349172407e8a40c0fc59d6c789119e7d","nod