ithub.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/653fd6c0610d40d2b744b09e9aec0c546342f8b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:27:11Z","email":"168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Watkins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:27:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(embedding): sync UnsavedChanges form to host updates when pristine (#85)\n\n* fix(embedding): sync UnsavedChanges form to host updates when pristine\n\nThe guest seeded its editable form from ui-state only on the first payload, so later host echoes updated the saved baseline while the form stayed frozen — an untouched form could flip to dirty and show a spurious Save/Discard bar. Now the form adopts host values whenever the user has nothing in progress (first payload, pristine form, or the echo from our own save), and preserves genuine in-progress edits. Fixed in both React and Angular guests with regression tests.\n\nCloses #81\n\n* test(embedding): cover the save-normalization echo and assert dirty state\n\nAdd a test where the host normalizes a saved value and echoes it back (the case the saving-adopt branch exists for) and assert the form adopts it without staying dirty. Also assert markDirtyState is not fired on a pristine background update — the actual regression symptom — and reword the adopt comment to drop a colon-introduced list.","tree":{"sha":"2a331021a247f34155c215e3194dfc681c32dac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/trees/2a331021a247f34155c215e3194dfc681c32dac0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/commits/653fd6c0610d40d2b744b09e9aec0c546342f8b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a331021a247f34155c215e3194dfc681c32dac0\nparent a4fe21cd8723cce265475a68a572fe53d4c045a6\nauthor Charles Watkins <168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com> 1790699231 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790699231 -0700\n\nfix(embedding): sync UnsavedChanges form to host updates when pristine (#85)\n\n* fix(embedding): sync UnsavedChanges form to host updates when pristine\n\nThe guest seeded its editable form from ui-state only on the first payload, so later host echoes updated the saved baseline while the form stayed frozen — an untouched form could flip to dirty and show a spurious Save/Discard bar. Now the form adopts host values whenever the user has nothing in progress (first payload, pristine form, or the echo from our own save), and preserves genuine in-progress edits. Fixed in both React and Angular guests with regression tests.\n\nCloses #81\n\n* test(embedding): cover the save-normalization echo and assert dirty state\n\nAdd a test where the host normalizes a saved value and echoes it back (the case the saving-adopt branch exists for) and assert the form adopts it without staying dirty. Also assert markDirtyState is not fired on a pristine background update — the actual regression symptom — and reword the adopt comment to drop a colon-introduced list.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu+bfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu5AQAFyH8yZUSiQbXXs/32SRR6DO\nv3JrAenXKT+q1vRCZscryEX/5Sflg6OdZg+b4e9ESYUxJe+qidsIDcea/bk1+rxG\nvGz3sTjcI/yXuC0ZQBmc3MT5of0+tBBypDACjljQ6yS8ITwk/pWF0IHc6dg/Ov5D\nVEjuy83ei0p1wVkBWKozc85W9Y5k1g9iD68VSFzZXbcHpBX49XEFQVUKJlYM0APs\n4qImIcFhZMoBQvOWzmAu5ejcQmrqEQKp1AFACu9OIArEGywJJtHrKbxpuJAwqY4f\nzPS0uGzmxgtokQDJ6CiZXyIQMM+zKzqiCNy3ov07FWw9+SKvQt/bPcSynqH2q0YJ\n24LzG1qkVCms+lko53ic6nAcIJd13vI7iSj5c1ybEU8Pvo0e6+XkryeLTptvl/SG\nMAswaHNSQNU+6TPlPq+9SAS0cB/CUh9M63HeWQTsU+kpSZu68TBXZOt0K3VNToso\nb3esR1i4pjTQWd6nKjSd54WQ4aglA2E97DgzzFAHRFPIGi5b0YoHEZa