er}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commit/05d5b12e053e0f93dc512b6bda3cdb7b5535d6f6","node_id":"C_kwDOSACgc9oAKDA1ZDViMTJlMDUzZTBmOTNkYzUxMmI2YmRhM2NkYjdiNTUzNWQ2ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commit/1ae3b1920f3634b9755112a4e9ae4b8f6608824f","sha":"1ae3b1920f3634b9755112a4e9ae4b8f6608824f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/1ae3b1920f3634b9755112a4e9ae4b8f6608824f"}],"sha":"05d5b12e053e0f93dc512b6bda3cdb7b5535d6f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/05d5b12e053e0f93dc512b6bda3cdb7b5535d6f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168678941?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesw-salesforce","id":168678941,"login":"charlesw-salesforce","node_id":"U_kgDOCg3WHQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/1ae3b1920f3634b9755112a4e9ae4b8f6608824f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T22:54:10Z","email":"168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Watkins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T22:54:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: wait for permission set group recalculation before assigning (#100)\n\n* ci: wait for permission set group recalculation before assigning\n\nA deployed PermissionSetGroup is recalculated asynchronously. CI runs\ndeploy and assign back-to-back, so recipesAll is sometimes still\nOutdated when the assign fires, failing with ''You can only assign users\nto permission set groups that have the \"Updated\" status.'' (seen on the\npost-merge CI for #99).\n\nPoll PermissionSetGroup.Status until it reaches Updated (bounded to ~2\nmin) before assigning, in both the push and PR workflows. The race is\nintermittent, so local runs can pass while CI fails.\n\n* docs: note permission set group recalculation wait in README\n\nThe default-deploy flow assigns recipesAll immediately after deploy, so a\nuser can hit the transient ''Updated status'' error while the permission\nset group is still recalculating. Add a tip to wait and retry.","tree":{"sha":"a9d98a3117fb3ca9bd17d006800cb6275c9501ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/trees/a9d98a3117fb3ca9bd17d006800cb6275c9501ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/commits/1ae3b1920f3634b9755112a4e9ae4b8f6608824f","verification":{"payload":"tree a9d98a3117fb3ca9bd17d006800cb6275c9501ed\nparent 7270b4c1a981853099cb118ea982bf986c4c733f\nauthor Charles Watkins <168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com> 1789426450 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789426450 -0700\n\nci: wait for permission set group recalculation before assigning (#100)\n\n* ci: wait for permission set group recalculation before assigning\n\nA deployed PermissionSetGroup is recalculated asynchronously. CI runs\ndeploy and assign back-to-back, so recipesAll is sometimes still\nOutdated when the assign fires, failing with ''You can only assign users\nto permission set groups that have the \"Updated\" status.'' (seen on the\npost-merge CI for #99).\n\nPoll PermissionSetGroup.Status until it reaches Updated (bounded to ~2\nmin) before assigning, in both the push and PR workflows. The race is\nintermittent, so local runs can pass while CI fails.\n\n* docs: note permission set group recalculation wait in README\n\nThe default-deploy flow assigns recipesAll immediately after deploy, so a\nuser can hit the transient ''Updated status'' error while the permission\nset group is still recalculating. Add a tip to wait and retry.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqHsSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALGIQAE+NwtunBHoXzKHQRzlUSaWD\nCaF2GruPncDdP/udlwTJkfEkIiDhZOa0pFJHAdPOtY9K1eQKF7+vqybegoDXwvSR\nTayQi9qucjfl6iEGFAfc/oEyClndabPAMiX1+id9PLgHOcLI0vNSELwe8WvOdOwu\n8lMh/nYF5ofMSvVNmMlxhAzWzPF1+eXbv0C/zMv/go3q3/N233szXlkJcenEFWwa\nqhKEwDwnxjdaipwhsQpJBnBQUYGwoHvhZZdsEOadtAEwp344Lou/cUJZbVV+vYI+\nBZJaMNLUIGG7npHtFhbq4nlKvbGhDlzFpVtp1FAjnOyvWEs35vrKiybiBRsg7bFm\no3Zx+cMggtgaiqAxlehPkjkf3mUDP0amwsM1vMTj2FILk2yj1+KFePmE9XQoVc7e\nx6GqmKv5ApE2NtE05SKIb46QsheTg2SApbrdNp00UvSKv/Wgqge14unkTKUiXvko\np0rySP+TnzDxxSYV9C6TvIRpSBq2dTqeVtwx21FYvszAZOQctnhHfm7ATpDd8T+y\nGT3qknfgEGQ2WSzut3Qnx+1KmgYDHXOLQkjdbLs/Dq8d1ti7z0XxoL0tKjbGn/ca\ntU4sKskCjgA4/WAE7Ng3TYT9+DkwYSybc/ep2CIiU358HJ0Sypwl711Di1amZcYT\nMhmBf0DPGEDu2gBvm/CJ\n=VLg8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T22:54:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commit/1ae3b1920f3634b9755112a4e9ae4b8f6608824f","node_id":"C_kwDOSACgc9oAKDFhZTNiMTkyMGYzNjM0Yjk3NTUxMTJhNGU5YWU0YjhmNjYwODgyNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commit/7270b4c1a981853099cb118ea982bf986c4c733f","sha":"7270b4c1a981853099cb118ea982bf986c4c733f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/7270b4c1a981853099cb118ea982bf986c4c733f"}],"sha":"1ae3b1920f3634b9755112a4e9ae4b8f6608824f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/1ae3b1920f3634b9755112a4e9ae4b8f6608824f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168678941?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesw-salesforce","id":168678941,"login":"charlesw-salesforce","node_id":"U_kgDOCg3WHQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/7270b4c1a981853099cb118ea982bf986c4c733f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:31:37Z","email":"168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Watkins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:31:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: make Angular and Micro-Frontends generally available (#99)\n\n* chore(deploy): ship all frameworks by default\n\nAngular and Micro-Frontend Recipes are now GA. Remove their\n.forceignore excludes so the standard deploy ships all three\nframework apps instead of React only.\n\n* refactor(permset): shared recipes set plus thin per-framework sets\n\nMake the shared ''recipes'' permission set focus on shared components:\ndrop the React app visibility and add ContactsResource Apex access. It\nnow carries only the shared object, field, tab, and Apex permissions.\n\nBreak the React app visibility out into a new thin ''reactRecipes'' set,\nmirroring ''angularRecipes'' and ''microfrontendRecipes''. Trim the\nduplicated object/field/tab permissions out of ''angularRecipes'' so every\nframework set layers on the shared ''recipes'' base.\n\n* refactor(app): move reactRecipes application into react-recipes package\n\nThe React custom application lived in the shared default/ tree while the\nAngular and Micro-Frontend apps live in their own package dirs. Move it\ninto force-app/main/react-recipes/applications so React mirrors the\nother frameworks. Metadata resolves by API name, so this is deploy-neutral.\n\n* feat(permset): add recipesAll permission set group\n\nAdd a Recipes (All Frameworks) permission set group that bundles the\nshared ''recipes'' set with the reactRecipes, angularRecipes, and\nmicrofrontendRecipes sets, so one assignment grants every recipe app.\n\n* docs: mark Angular and Micro-Frontend recipes as GA\n\nAngular and Micro-Frontend Recipes are generally available. Remove all\npreview / work-in-progress / Developer Preview language and the\n.forceignore opt-in steps across the root and per-app READMEs.\n\nSimplify the default deploy: ship all of force-app and assign the new\nrecipesAll permission set group in one step. Add per-framework\ninstructions for deploying and assigning a single framework on its own\n(shared ''recipes'' set plus that framework''s thin set). Update the README\nstructure ruleset accordingly.\n\n* ci: build all frameworks and assign recipesAll before deploy\n\nWith Angular and Micro-Frontend no longer force-ignored, the default\ndeploy ships every framework, so CI must build the Angular UI bundle\ntoo. Add Angular install/build steps before deploy and switch the\npermission assignment to the recipesAll group in both CI workflows.\n\n* refactor(app): rename Micro-Frontend app to microfrontendRecipes\n\nThe Micro-Frontend CustomApplication used the API name MicrofrontendRecipes\nwhile the React and Angular apps (reactRecipes, angularRecipes) and the\nMicro-Frontend permission set itself (microfrontendRecipes) all use\nlowerCamelCase. Rename the app to microfrontendRecipes for consistency and\nupdate the permission set''s applicationVisibilities reference. The app label\n(Micro-Frontend Recipes) is unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"ca9103dfc6fa896637eb409bed73541ec40b7280","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/trees/ca9103dfc6fa896637eb409bed73541ec40b7280"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/commits/7270b4c1a981853099cb118ea982bf986c4c733f","verification":{"payload":"tree ca9103dfc6fa896637eb409bed73541ec40b7280\nparent 7cb4b6efed787d444fa5e564ff789a1da16edf41\nauthor Charles Watkins <168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com> 1789410697 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789410697 -0700\n\nfeat: make Angular and Micro-Frontends generally available (#99)\n\n* chore(deploy): ship all frameworks by default\n\nAngular and Micro-Frontend Recipes are now GA. Remove their\n.forceignore excludes so the standard deploy ships all three\nframework apps instead of React only.\n\n* refactor(permset): shared recipes set plus thin per-framework sets\n\nMake the shared ''recipes'' permission set focus on shared components:\ndrop the React app visibility and add ContactsResource Apex access. It\nnow carries only the shared object, field, tab, and Apex permissions.\n\nBreak the React app visibility out into a new thin ''reactRecipes'' set,\nmirroring ''angularRecipes'' and ''microfrontendRecipes''. Trim the\nduplicated object/field/tab permissions out of ''angularRecipes'' so every\nframework set layers on the shared ''recipes'' base.\n\n* refactor(app): move reactRecipes application into react-recipes package\n\nThe React custom application lived in the shared default/ tree while the\nAngular and Micro-Frontend apps live in their own package dirs. Move it\ninto force-app/main/react-recipes/applications so React mirrors the\nother frameworks. Metadata resolves by API name, so this is deploy-neutral.\n\n* feat(permset): add recipesAll permission set group\n\nAdd a Recipes (All Frameworks) permission set group that bundles the\nshared ''recipes'' set with the reactRecipes, angularRecipes, and\nmicrofrontendRecipes sets, so one assignment grants every recipe app.\n\n* docs: mark Angular and Micro-Frontend recipes as GA\n\nAngular and Micro-Frontend Recipes are generally available. Remove all\npreview / work-in-progress / Developer Preview language and the\n.forceignore opt-in steps across the root and per-app READMEs.\n\nSimplify the default deploy: ship all of force-app and assign the new\nrecipesAll permission set group in one step. Add per-framework\ninstructions for deploying and assigning a single framework on its own\n(shared ''recipes'' set plus that framework''s thin set). Update the README\nstructure ruleset accordingly.\n\n* ci: build all frameworks and assign recipesAll before deploy\n\nWith Angular and Micro-Frontend no longer force-ignored, the default\ndeploy ships every framework, so CI must build the Angular UI bundle\ntoo. Add Angular install/build steps before deploy and switch the\npermission assignment to the recipesAll group in both CI workflows.\n\n* refactor(app): rename Micro-Frontend app to microfrontendRecipes\n\nThe Micro-Frontend CustomApplication used the API name MicrofrontendRecipes\nwhile the React and Angular apps (reactRecipes, angularRecipes) and the\nMicro-Frontend permission set itself (microfrontendRecipes) all use\nlowerCamelCase. Rename the app to microfrontendRecipes for consistency and\nupdate the permission set''s applicationVisibilities reference. The app label\n(Micro-Frontend Recipes) is unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqD2JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ5YQAALDbnegdhQjvr6EcP2AQLFH\n1qncQafZsm3lpKIgGDXqZe/h+PHdy2J3flr2oyAWQnTLmvgdmHOn/qEPHo4XBguv\nXUIAA3UDqRrVhCErcePqve+3+sMpHNLEgysrzxV7BR66AnbtL1nHmvD0/goEkXlR\n+ShAPQZ1zsjhSefUSbHCOhpyEE/rohVFsZkCNgJXFJNDUjZ22x9MZaLuce+xVajE\npIypfWH8KMaE8L2qPOivCHZ82zp6OG8v+IPvNz8E2dXM9Ycx12w8emoRH+ckH6GR\n1h2LSwvpiaXtrZSwWxrKR4S9+3/YOd3G1nYyzVPfm/fCz/sJjjVz6AhlCYkKvsVL\ngJydSko+GAE24/e/Oq18O2ApHb1zVtSGkbtR/CM7bz7YKZbZeiR16MshCFu83JeW\noja3p89tzwBv7oQipzh/WyMrQw11YcjYsbQG86WbQnmHTwJXRk1AtCQi5+IphGNK\ntmfqe5CCcnXXVtkDkQvK0joPNkdWpo+M/Y4Y4qU+0LqSq+KoCKcyijCUWK7y4Xsu\n7q2EfsD/UfmJccrQW7oquHa2HjVDzGjelKkVnf9W1pJe3RU9GMLZt150teHW5BiI\nZJhnQ1I5SssFvHtygVUMDpYOmCYPk+7T8PWIGf4APeBkE2rLfviGjsxwO+/9MUcv\nST5NKgUN2aCMUniE+jEi\n=n7Ru\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verif