ype":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commit/dee6c43b0123ff1339835ccc7317332aaf2ca927","node_id":"C_kwDOSACgc9oAKGRlZTZjNDNiMDEyM2ZmMTMzOTgzNWNjYzczMTczMzJhYWYyY2E5Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commit/0b54d8a26de86105fc52f938113422c1f2f9a646","sha":"0b54d8a26de86105fc52f938113422c1f2f9a646","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/0b54d8a26de86105fc52f938113422c1f2f9a646"}],"sha":"dee6c43b0123ff1339835ccc7317332aaf2ca927","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/dee6c43b0123ff1339835ccc7317332aaf2ca927"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168678941?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesw-salesforce","id":168678941,"login":"charlesw-salesforce","node_id":"U_kgDOCg3WHQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/0b54d8a26de86105fc52f938113422c1f2f9a646/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T20:27:44Z","email":"168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Watkins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T20:27:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(angular): add recipe all categories (#75)\n\n* feat(angular): add shared UI primitives for the recipes\n\nField, input, label, and select primitives (app-* wrappers over spartan-ng hlm), plus recipe helpers (skeleton, stat-card) and the icons the ported categories use.\n\n* feat(angular): add Read Data recipes\n\nUIAPI GraphQL queries: single record, list, filtered/debounced, sorted, cursor pagination, related records, aliased multi-object, and imperative refetch.\n\n* feat(angular): add Modify Data recipes\n\nUIAPI GraphQL mutations: create, update, delete, server-side error handling, and query + mutation together.\n\n* feat(angular): add Salesforce APIs recipes\n\nREST beyond GraphQL via sdk.fetch: current user (Chatter), UI API REST, and custom Apex REST.\n\n* feat(angular): add Integration recipes\n\nEnd-to-end patterns: debounced searchable account list and an aliased multi-object dashboard.\n\n* feat(angular): add Error Handling recipes\n\nLoading/error/empty states, containing failures without a render boundary, and reading GraphQL errors.\n\n* feat(angular): add Styling recipes\n\nSLDS blueprint classes and sprites alongside the app''s spartan-ng components and Lucide icons.\n\n* feat(angular): add Routing recipes\n\nAngular Router in a UI Bundle: routerLink, active links, programmatic navigation, route parameters, and nested routes.\n\n* feat(angular): register recipes and wire routes, nav, and home\n\nRoute and register the seven categories, add component input binding for route params, and surface the categories as Home tiles.\n\n* docs(angular): document the ported recipes\n\nRecipe catalog table, learning path, and hero image.\n\n* build(angular): upgrade @salesforce/* to 12.x for React parity\n\nBump @salesforce/platform-sdk, @salesforce/ui-bundle, and @salesforce/angular-plugin-ui-bundle from 11.62 to ^12.3.3 to match React Recipes and pick up the embedding view SDK surface (getViewSDK, ui-embedding).\n\n* feat(angular): add badge primitive and embedding icons\n\nHand-build an app-badge wrapper (spartan-ng ships no badge) and register the lucide glyphs the embedding recipes need in APP_ICONS.\n\n* feat(angular): add chromeless guest layout for embedded recipes\n\nGuestLayout toggles .embedding-guest and imports the ui-embedding bootstrap at load; styles.css makes the guest surface transparent and marginless so only the recipe shows inside the host iframe.\n\n* feat(angular): add micro-frontend embedding guest recipes\n\nSeven guest recipes ported from React Recipes — basic render, read host data, send to host, unsaved changes, theme tokens, auto resize, and receive event — each a chromeless standalone component with a co-located spec, exchanging ui-state and events with the host via getViewSDK().\n\n* feat(angular): add embedding catalog page and wire routing and nav\n\nAdd the bespoke /embedding catalog, register the chromeless embedding/<slug> guest routes (matched before the shell so its ** catch-all doesn''t swallow them), and surface the catalog through a Micro-Frontends navbar link and a Home callout — mirroring React''s entry points.\n\n* docs(angular): document embedding guest routes and dev server port\n\nNote the /embedding guest routes and catalog, the localhost:5173 dev server, and how the microfrontend-recipes LWC hosts embed the guests.\n\n* test(angular): isolate specs to stop cross-file mock bleed\n\nThe unit-test builder ran specs without module isolation, so vi.mock(''@salesforce/platform-sdk'') leaked between files — a store could read another spec''s mocked query (flaky ''expected length 1, got 2'' in nested-routes-store). Add vitest-base.config.ts (via runnerConfig) with isolate:true so each spec''s mocks stay hermetic; file parallelism is kept, so the suite stays fast.\n\n* feat(angular): add embedding GraphQL Data guest recipe\n\nPort React''s new GraphqlData guest (#84): the indirect-org-access pattern where the host runs one GraphQL query for the account''s related Contacts and pushes the rows down as a contactsdata event, which the guest requests via requestcontacts and renders. Adds the guest + spec, briefcase/mail icons, the catalog entry, and the chromeless route.","tree":{"sha":"3b50fa5451272fe8e7eeff3f27c71bf777fea3d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/trees/3b50fa5451272fe8e7eeff3f27c71bf777fea3d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/commits/0b54d8a26de86105fc52f938113422c1f2f9a646","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b50fa5451272fe8e7eeff3f27c71bf777fea3d7\nparent ce41f15114dfa8ec2773fdc94f2c5125122ef550\nauthor Charles Watkins <168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com> 1788899264 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788899264 -0700\n\nfeat(angular): add recipe all categories (#75)\n\n* feat(angular): add shared UI primitives for the recipes\n\nField, input, label, and select primitives (app-* wrappers over spartan-ng hlm), plus recipe helpers (skeleton, stat-card) and the icons the ported categories use.\n\n* feat(angular): add Read Data recipes\n\nUIAPI GraphQL queries: single record, list, filtered/debounced, sorted, cursor pagination, related records, aliased multi-object, and imperative refetch.\n\n* feat(angular): add Modify Data recipes\n\nUIAPI GraphQL mutations: create, update, delete, server-side error handling, and query + mutation together.\n\n* feat(angular): add Salesforce APIs recipes\n\nREST beyond GraphQL via sdk.fetch: current user (Chatter), UI API REST, and custom Apex REST.\n\n* feat(angular): add Integration recipes\n\nEnd-to-end patterns: debounced searchable account list and an aliased multi-object dashboard.\n\n* feat(angular): add Error Handling recipes\n\nLoading/error/empty states, containing failures without a render boundary, and reading GraphQL errors.\n\n* feat(angular): add Styling recipes\n\nSLDS blueprint classes and sprites alongside the app''s spartan-ng components and Lucide icons.\n\n* feat(angular): add Routing recipes\n\nAngular Router in a UI Bundle: routerLink, active links, programmatic navigation, route parameters, and nested routes.\n\n* feat(angular): register recipes and wire routes, nav, and home\n\nRoute and register the seven categories, add component input binding for route params, and surface the categories as Home tiles.\n\n* docs(angular): document the ported recipes\n\nRecipe catalog table, learning path, and hero image.\n\n* build(angular): upgrade @salesforce/* to 12.x for React parity\n\nBump @salesforce/platform-sdk, @salesforce/ui-bundle, and @salesforce/angular-plugin-ui-bundle from 11.62 to ^12.3.3 to match React Recipes and pick up the embedding view SDK surface (getViewSDK, ui-embedding).\n\n* feat(angular): add badge primitive and embedding icons\n\nHand-build an app-badge wrapper (spartan-ng ships no badge) and register the lucide glyphs the embedding recipes need in APP_ICONS.\n\n* feat(angular): add chromeless guest layout for embedded recipes\n\nGuestLayout toggles .embedding-guest and imports the ui-embedding bootstrap at load; styles.css makes the guest surface transparent and marginless so only the recipe shows inside the host iframe.\n\n* feat(angular): add micro-frontend embedding guest recipes\n\nSeven guest recipes ported from React Recipes — basic render, read host data, send to host, unsaved changes, theme tokens, auto resize, and receive event — each a chromeless standalone component with a co-located spec, exchanging ui-state and events with the host via getViewSDK().\n\n* feat(angular): add embedding catalog page and wire routing and nav\n\nAdd the bespoke /embedding catalog, register the chromeless embedding/<slug> guest routes (matched before the shell so its ** catch-all doesn''t swallow them), and surface the catalog through a Micro-Frontends navbar link and a Home callout — mirroring React''s entry points.\n\n* docs(angular): document embedding guest routes and dev server port\n\nNote the /embedding guest routes and catalog, the localhost:5173 dev server, and how the microfrontend-recipes LWC hosts embed the guests.\n\n* test(angular): isolate specs to stop cross-file mock bleed\n\nThe unit-test builder ran specs without module isolation, so vi.mock(''@salesforce/platform-sdk'') leaked between files — a store could read another spec''s mocked query (flaky ''expected length 1, got 2'' in nested-routes-store). Add vitest-base.config.ts (via runnerConfig) with isolate:true so each spec''s mocks stay hermetic; file parallelism is kept, so the suite stays fast.\n\n* feat(angular): add embedding GraphQL Data guest recipe\n\nPort React''s new GraphqlData guest (#84): the indirect-org-access pattern where the host runs one GraphQL query for the account''s related Contacts and pushes the rows down as a contactsdata event, which the guest requests via requestcontacts and renders. Adds the guest + spec, briefcase/mail icons, the catalog entry, and the chromeless route.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoG/ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxv0QADS+aU/evvhyLqim5BpL5/2q\n/etc+ldgiUSYsFA4/WHD62BK3zi0XrjVtfJRH8TcnsnufngXKErR4MKrIhfdb8nB\nEpU9uWBtYMr7lpuQ+MC5VNyLRMdpw3yZi3cZF6jUuxn3y7liiikxbfaNARpFcxM7\nwhRAgDYSgEfvmWUggIiDkpXlYe5Ildcci1cGFgymysPJt0rgp9emJtseDqSKIBvc\nQFEj5oiq9UreKDt/78kbI3j2jNr8oLjun4ZMMo9fW1vOjlD76GYo7bWpNw+Ce4o0\nGfpSUgYChi4G+0fMX2KQIho1VWhiJ6TAUpd9ZFpnkcd6303lpb1QKhHv593XP26j\nsj6YLluResihQMfoILU/tGgOcxx4A/gadvlJXPAfxQzJL3FrJL0ByVzm8YoBZql1\nW3dl7n2Q2Kenutp9yOoYve/zx7a7v72ArdkT+cz86I2Ueou4Wh6zckB1FKgFaEzl\nY0KhrUX5GLMuPSo3eumy7qMCBRreOGALL7l1EJNIaVrMD06aO/ggJk+lTx40paCH\neWDNS65jVW3GgedvIik0IXK3Sh/AjzqUJZdqIeJKVNY2+jp8cCZsSjYN3Ejr7pex\nzcQJn5H/8ujlaXSbXFlHEZvIdNMq53KF3YIPftB4USGl1U/nNyMYXj9pxxSx6w