bscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commit/ea9c252a8ebc25b4a5c9e99af8b9a8b8bb449bc3","node_id":"C_kwDOSACgc9oAKGVhOWMyNTJhOGViYzI1YjRhNWM5ZTk5YWY4YjlhOGI4YmI0NDliYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commit/8f65d0b2f44c45bdb5949226a268ae9620fd494a","sha":"8f65d0b2f44c45bdb5949226a268ae9620fd494a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/8f65d0b2f44c45bdb5949226a268ae9620fd494a"}],"sha":"ea9c252a8ebc25b4a5c9e99af8b9a8b8bb449bc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/ea9c252a8ebc25b4a5c9e99af8b9a8b8bb449bc3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168678941?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesw-salesforce","id":168678941,"login":"charlesw-salesforce","node_id":"U_kgDOCg3WHQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesw-salesforce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/commits/8f65d0b2f44c45bdb5949226a268ae9620fd494a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-20T21:27:15Z","email":"168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Watkins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-20T21:27:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add Windows build to CI (#14)\n\n* fix: use explicit module augmentation for vitest-axe types (#13)\n\nReplace /// <reference types=\"vitest-axe/extend-expect\" /> with an\nexplicit declare module augmentation to fix TypeScript build failures\non Windows where the reference directive fails to resolve.\n\n* fix: switch from @testing-library/jest-dom to @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest (#13)\n\n* fix: use explicit module augmentation for vitest-axe types (#13)\n\nReplace /// <reference types> directives with import statements for\ncross-platform compatibility. Add Windows CI job to catch platform-\nspecific type resolution issues.\n\n* test: revert vitest-env.d.ts to original reference directives to test Windows CI\n\n* fix: use imports instead of reference directives for type augmentation (#13)\n\n* refactor: extract Windows build into reusable workflow (#15)\n\n- Deduplicate the windows-build job from ci.yml and ci-pr.yml into a\n  shared workflow_call workflow\n- Use node-version-file instead of hardcoding Node 22 to stay in sync\n  with the Volta config in package.json\n- Add node_modules caching via actions/cache for faster CI runs\n- Use npm run test instead of bare npx vitest for consistency with\n  the Linux CI job\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mohith Shrivastava <msrivastav13@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"42e821578e46131f8c38aa83f16acc11ec49cb40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/trees/42e821578e46131f8c38aa83f16acc11ec49cb40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trailheadapps/multiframework-recipes/git/commits/8f65d0b2f44c45bdb5949226a268ae9620fd494a","verification":{"payload":"tree 42e821578e46131f8c38aa83f16acc11ec49cb40\nparent 30935ba6c0a17a44c3a7e13a2d3a77b8020e7e92\nauthor Charles Watkins <168678941+charlesw-salesforce@users.noreply.github.com> 1779312435 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779312435 -0700\n\nAdd Windows build to CI (#14)\n\n* fix: use explicit module augmentation for vitest-axe types (#13)\n\nReplace /// <reference types=\"vitest-axe/extend-expect\" /> with an\nexplicit declare module augmentation to fix TypeScript build failures\non Windows where the reference directive fails to resolve.\n\n* fix: switch from @testing-library/jest-dom to @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest (#13)\n\n* fix: use explicit module augmentation for vitest-axe types (#13)\n\nReplace /// <reference types> directives with import statements for\ncross-platform compatibility. Add Windows CI job to catch platform-\nspecific type resolution issues.\n\n* test: revert vitest-env.d.ts to original reference directives to test Windows CI\n\n* fix: use imports instead of reference directives for type augmentation (#13)\n\n* refactor: extract Windows build into reusable workflow (#15)\n\n- Deduplicate the windows-build job from ci.yml and ci-pr.yml into a\n  shared workflow_call workflow\n- Use node-version-file instead of hardcoding Node 22 to stay in sync\n  with the Volta config in package.json\n- Add node_modules caching via actions/cache for faster CI runs\n- Use npm run test instead of bare npx vitest for consistency with\n  the Linux CI job\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mohith Shrivastava <msrivastav13@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDiczCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/NQQAF8pQoB5B7DXqT2SHAdOxgAH\nCFH7hgbImfEZ9xGof139aackWSQBDDF5GSJoKLEzV6vQtQS/rkn0SCUNOuCUgwWR\nXvG6AeJ1TYJ/xHYkqRA4lkwqMArUu88ho/HxcRYz7YUGdTpHb/KBdMKbybLGH3ct\n55O4l5D3u/5V8MpSIwlpbQwRNSUi8jp/DeEWD6dvzyo4l3zrnvvCmPKx7CbO9Y2T\nTHx5zj1eMuxpxTXVdXGNuSs+giYQM2KCl9FhKp7nCGWrBacb6j/ADtyRJnCKlnNO\n2hOuSvXDzQck+bsDzbxJGfHpwLgn/26+i3fhUoK399YQJOdcqq3/uDsb9/5sD/vM\nEUusgHDtxouSphnjzW64xAHAIKJcJjSMHWglNR6M7w2hOogbj4t/kcRmj