github.com/users/abailey81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/commits/8708d20617442baa530cd4434714d1df62ef9c4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:14:08Z","email":"tamer.atesyakar@bk.ru","name":"Tamer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:14:08Z","email":"tamer.atesyakar@bk.ru","name":"Tamer"},"message":"docs(complete-guide): add priority levels (P0–P3) to every section\n\nTriage tags so the user can read by available time:\n- P0 CRITICAL — must memorise; quoted nearly verbatim in interview.\n- P1 HIGH — strongly should know; high probability of coming up.\n- P2 MEDIUM — good to know; depends on interviewer angle.\n- P3 REFERENCE — only look up if asked / if you blank.\n\nTriage paths laid out at the top:\n- 30 min the morning of → every P0.\n- 90 min (recommended) → every P0 + P1.\n- 3+ hours (gold standard) → everything.\n\nTags applied to:\n- Every Part header (0–19)\n- Every subsection (5.1–5.11, 9.1–9.10, 11.1–11.4, 12.x, 13.x)\n- Table of Contents (extended to cover Parts 12–19 which were\n  missing from the original ToC)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f34584dee807d23a4c224110c78abce104f797bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/git/trees/f34584dee807d23a4c224110c78abce104f797bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/git/commits/8708d20617442baa530cd4434714d1df62ef9c4c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166416725?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/us