repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/commits/cf89fafa40d56f6f8a7dbb5cf847877f9a2af381/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:03:49Z","email":"tamer.atesyakar@bk.ru","name":"Tamer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T23:03:49Z","email":"tamer.atesyakar@bk.ru","name":"Tamer"},"message":"docs: complete pre-interview guide\n\nSingle-file, end-to-end interview prep:\n- Parts 1-2: 60-second pitch + Huawei context\n- Part 3: 25 foundational concepts (transformer, BPE, LoRA, DoRA,\n  NEFTune, MoE, ACT, TCN, ONNX, INT8, contextual bandit, …)\n  introduced from first principles\n- Parts 4-5: full architecture top-down + 11-component deep-dive\n  (SLM, Qwen LoRA, Gemini, TCN, smart router, 14-stage pipeline,\n  edge deployment, Identity Lock, privacy, actuators, KG)\n- Part 6: locked source-of-truth numbers (every value pinned to\n  the verifier)\n- Part 7: 10-minute live-demo walkthrough\n- Part 8: six PR-shaped open problems with effort estimates\n- Part 9: 10 Q&A sub-banks (recruiter pre-screen, architecture,\n  SLM, fine-tuning, edge, HCI, privacy, honest-gaps, behavioural,\n  curveball)\n- Part 10: 65-term glossary\n- Part 11: file paths + 27 papers + five-things-to-quote-no-matter-what\n- Part 12: interview-day playbook (pacing, body language, blank-rescue)\n- Part 13: questions to ask THEM (and ones to avoid)\n- Part 14: 20 ML fundamentals you should be able to discuss\n- Part 15: 7 whiteboard / coding scenarios with skeleton code\n- Part 16: 10 hard-moment recovery scripts\n- Part 17: logistics scripts (visa, salary, start date)\n- Part 18: morning-of checklist\n\nDesigned to be the only document the user needs the morning of.\n