github.com/users/abailey81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/commits/81231f5153044bbaf2de36b3851d74ace31a719a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:07:58Z","email":"tamer.atesyakar@bk.ru","name":"Tamer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T22:07:58Z","email":"tamer.atesyakar@bk.ru","name":"Tamer"},"message":"docs: numbers audit — fix every drift caught against verify_numbers.py\n\nTriggered by zip-submission to a downstream Claude reviewer; precision\nmust be 100 %.  Re-derived the ground truth from disk, then walked\nevery recruiter-facing .md against the verifier.\n\nFixes\n- README.md\n  * Corpus pairs 974,610 → **977,332** (count from triples.json source field)\n  * Source breakdown table: replaced rounded counts with real per-source\n    counts (Cornell 206 k, SQuAD 87 k, DailyDialog 81 k, PersonaChat\n    128 k, WikiText 242 k, OpenSubs 227 k, curated overlay 6 k)\n  * v2 SLM eval row: replaced stale \"407 → 148 over 16 k steps\" with the\n    actual `best_eval_loss = 4.987` (perplexity ≈ 147) at step 18 000,\n    plus the stress-test framing (≈ 1 725 on n=500 full-corpus)\n  * Re-headed v1 / v2 sections so default-loaded label is correct\n  * §4 edge claim now leads with the live INT8 ONNX encoder (162.2 KB,\n    parity MAE 0.00055, browser-side via onnxruntime-web)\n\n- docs/TECHNICAL_REPORT.md\n  * Same corpus and perplexity drift as above\n  * Replaced the synthetic training-curve table with the verifiable\n    end-points (`best_eval_loss = 4.987`, step 18 000, plus stress-test)\n\n- docs/huawei/slm_artefact.md\n  * `n_experts (MoE) | 4` → **2** (matches checkpoint config)\n  * `max_seq_len | 1024` → **512** (matches checkpoint config)\n  * Section 4.1 \"Latest run\": stale n=200 numbers (ce 7.42, ppl 1 674.8,\n    top-1 10.24 %, tokens 13 228, wall 38.3 s, throughput 345 tok/s)\n    replaced with the actual n=500 run from `reports/slm_v2_eval.json`\n    (ce 7.4531, ppl 1 725.3, top-1 10.27 %, tokens 33 909, wall 84.3 s,\n    throughput 402 tok/s) plus correct per-quartile token counts\n  * Eval-loss precision tightened to 4.987 (was 4.99)\n  * Calibration note rewritten — now correctly explains the 1 725 vs 147\n    gap as distribution shift + history-token loss, not curated-overlay\n    narrowness\n\n- docs/huawei/jd_to_repo_map.md\n  * Corrected three rows that said \"Qwen3.5-2B + LoRA\" to **Qwen3-1.7B**\n    (the actual trained artefact; the script defaults to 3.5-2B and\n    falls back to 3-1.7B because transformers 4.57 doesn''t yet recognise\n    the 3.5 model_type — clarified inline)\n\n- docs/huawei/email_response.md\n  * Tokeniser claim \"32 k vocab trained on 974 k pairs\" → 977 k\n\n- docs/huawei/interview_talking_points.md\n  * Section 5.3 reframed from defending the v1 word-level tokenizer to\n    explaining the v2 byte-level BPE choice (which is what shipped)\n\n- scripts/verify_numbers.py\n  * Tightened corpus-size assertion from \"974 000 ± 5 000\" to the exact\n    977 332 (now any future drift in triples.json fails the audit\n    immediately)\n\nVerifier still 22 / 22 PASS after all changes.  Run\n`python scripts/verify_numbers.py` to confirm.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8b5a1cbc61e8822d9afb248546f8c415e7983d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/git/trees/c8b5a1cbc61e8822d9afb248546f8c415e7983d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/git/commits/81231f5153044bbaf2de36b3851d74ace31a719a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166416725?v=4","events_url":"h