ions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/commits/3fc4549e983196ca23da5a8db76fd0145e29a63b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T03:03:26Z","email":"tamer.atesyakar@bk.ru","name":"Tamer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T03:03:26Z","email":"tamer.atesyakar@bk.ru","name":"Tamer"},"message":"iter 123: CostTracker thread-safety + concurrent-record correctness\n\n4 tests pin the iter-67 CostTracker against concurrent updates from\nmultiple cloud-call threads (a real production concern when several\nWebSocket sessions issue cloud calls simultaneously).\n\nTESTS (4 / 4 green in 0.34 s)\n- 8 threads × 50 records each → exactly 400 calls counted, exact\n  prompt/completion token totals (no lost increments under racing).\n- Concurrent get_global_cost_tracker() returns the same singleton\n  instance across all 8 threads (double-checked-lock holds).\n- Two-record total_cost_usd == c1 + c2 (no torn writes).\n- reset_during_record_does_not_corrupt — reset between two records\n  starts fresh.\n\nTotal iter-52..123 test count: 579 / 579 green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"096a34d23ca0d85cc744793a0654df1c413536af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/git/trees/096a34d23ca0d85cc744793a0654df1c413536af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abailey81/implicit-interaction-intelligence/git/commits/3fc4549e983196ca23da5a8db76fd0145e29a63b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166416725?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abailey81/followi